    block is asked to give, named by its DxfAttributeDefinition.Tag, with its DxfAttributeDefinition.Prompt and
    default value."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        """Initializes an attribute definition with no tag, prompt or value at the origin, 2.5 high, as AutoCAD's
        new AttributeDefinition(), in no file; give it its tag before it is added to a block."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, position: GeoPoint3, value: str, tag: str, prompt: str, style: DxfTextStyleTableRecord) -> None:
        """Initializes an attribute definition, as AutoCAD's new AttributeDefinition(position, value, tag, prompt,
        style): at a point, with its default value, tag and prompt, 2.5 high, in a text style, in no file until
        it is added to a block."""
    @property
    def Constant(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute's value is fixed, the same in every INSERT (flag 2 of group 70), as
        AutoCAD's Constant."""
    @Constant.setter
    def Constant(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def FieldLength(self) -> int:
        """Gets or sets the length of the attribute's field (group 73), as AutoCAD's FieldLength; nought where the
        record gives none."""
    @FieldLength.setter
    def FieldLength(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Invisible(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute is not drawn (flag 1 of group 70), as AutoCAD's Invisible."""
    @Invisible.setter
    def Invisible(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def IsMTextAttributeDefinition(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute is a text of several lines, an MTEXT embedded in its record (group
        101), as AutoCAD's IsMTextAttributeDefinition."""
    @IsMTextAttributeDefinition.setter
    def IsMTextAttributeDefinition(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def LockPositionInBlock(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute keeps its place in the block when the block is edited (the group 280
        after its tag), as AutoCAD's LockPositionInBlock; false where the record gives none."""
    @LockPositionInBlock.setter
    def LockPositionInBlock(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def MTextAttributeDefinition(self) -> DxfMText:
        """Gets or sets the MTEXT the definition is made of where it is of several lines, as AutoCAD's
        MTextAttributeDefinition: as DxfAttributeReference.MTextAttribute gets and sets one, its type (71) 4, as
        ezdxf writes the definition of an attribute of several lines, but its default value (group 1) the MTEXT's
        contents, its lines apart by \\P, as AutoCAD 2021 writes the definition of three lines it makes: LINE
        ONE\\PLINE TWO\\PLINE THREE, where ezdxf writes the first line. DxfDBText.TextString reads the words of
        its lines joined by spaces, LINE ONE LINE TWO LINE THREE, as AutoCAD 2021 reads them, and an ATTRIB
        filled from the definition is given those."""
    @MTextAttributeDefinition.setter
    def MTextAttributeDefinition(self, value: DxfMText) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Preset(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute takes its default value without asking (flag 8 of group 70), as
        AutoCAD's Preset."""
    @Preset.setter
    def Preset(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Prompt(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets what an INSERT of the block is asked for the attribute (group 3), as AutoCAD's Prompt; empty
        where the record gives none."""
    @Prompt.setter
    def Prompt(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Tag(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the tag of the attribute (group 2), as AutoCAD's Tag: the name an INSERT's ATTRIB of it has,
        such as TAG1."""
    @Tag.setter
    def Tag(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Verifiable(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute's value is checked when it is given (flag 4 of group 70), as AutoCAD's
        Verifiable."""
    @Verifiable.setter
    def Verifiable(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    def UpdateMTextAttributeDefinition(self) -> None:
        """Places the definition's MTEXT where its text stands, as AutoCAD's UpdateMTextAttributeDefinition, as
        DxfAttributeReference.UpdateMTextAttribute places an attribute's; nothing for a definition of one line."""

class DxfAttributeReference(DxfDBText):
    """An ATTRIB of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's AttributeReference: the value an INSERT gives one of its block's
    attributes, a text of the INSERT's own named by its DxfAttributeReference.Tag, reached through
    DxfBlockReference.AttributeCollection."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        """Initializes an attribute with no tag or value at the origin, 2.5 high, as AutoCAD's new
        AttributeReference(), in no file; give it its tag, or fill it from its definition, before it is added to
        an INSERT."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, position: GeoPoint3, value: str, tag: str, style: DxfTextStyleTableRecord) -> None:
        """Initializes an attribute, as AutoCAD's new AttributeReference(position, value, tag, style): at a point,
        with its value and tag, 2.5 high, in a text style, in no file until it is added to an INSERT."""
    @property
    def FieldLength(self) -> int:
        """Gets or sets the length of the attribute's field (group 73), as AutoCAD's FieldLength; nought where the
        record gives none."""
    @FieldLength.setter
    def FieldLength(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Invisible(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute is not drawn (flag 1 of group 70), as AutoCAD's Invisible."""
    @Invisible.setter
    def Invisible(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def IsConstant(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the attribute's value is fixed by its definition (flag 2 of group 70), as AutoCAD's
        IsConstant."""
    @property
    def IsMTextAttribute(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute is a text of several lines, an MTEXT embedded in its record (group
        101), as AutoCAD's IsMTextAttribute."""
    @IsMTextAttribute.setter
    def IsMTextAttribute(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def IsPreset(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the attribute takes its default value without asking (flag 8 of group 70), as AutoCAD's
        IsPreset."""
    @property
    def IsVerifiable(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the attribute's value is checked when it is given (flag 4 of group 70), as AutoCAD's
        IsVerifiable."""
    @property
    def LockPositionInBlock(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the attribute keeps its place in the block when the block is edited (the group 280
        after its tag), as AutoCAD's LockPositionInBlock; false where the record gives none."""
    @LockPositionInBlock.setter
    def LockPositionInBlock(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def MTextAttribute(self) -> DxfMText:
        """Gets or sets the MTEXT the attribute is made of where it is of several lines, as AutoCAD's
        MTextAttribute."""
    @MTextAttribute.setter
    def MTextAttribute(self, value: DxfMText) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Tag(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the tag of the attribute (group 2), as AutoCAD's Tag: the name its block's definition gives
        it, such as TAG1."""
    @Tag.setter
    def Tag(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @overload
    def SetAttributeFromBlock(self, blockTransform: GeoTransform3) -> None:
        """Places the attribute again from its definition, as AutoCAD's SetAttributeFromBlock of one transformation
        does: the definition of its tag in the block its INSERT places, by
        DxfAttributeReference.SetAttributeFromBlock."""
    @overload
    def SetAttributeFromBlock(self, definition: DxfAttributeDefinition, blockTransform: GeoTransform3) -> None:
        """Fills the attribute from its definition in a block, as AutoCAD's SetAttributeFromBlock: the definition's
        text (its words as the default value, its height, rotation, alignment, style and the rest), tag, flags,
        field length and lock, and its look, then placed by the transformation that places the block, an INSERT's
        DxfBlockReference.BlockTransform. Its prompt is not an attribute's and is left out. A definition of
        several lines gives its embedded MTEXT and makes the attribute one of several lines, its type (71) 2
        where the definition's is 4, as ezdxf writes them, its value the words of every line of that MTEXT joined
        by spaces, as AutoCAD 2021 writes it. A definition not aligned left on its baseline gives its alignment
        point placed, the origin where its record has none: centred on (0, 0) in a block an INSERT places at
        (6000, 1000), it gives an attribute held by (6000, 1000), written 11 6000 21 1000, as AutoCAD 2021 gave
        it (check D30). An annotative attribute is placed so in the context it is shown at (DxfDBText.Position),
        its other contexts left as they were, and its record where that context is the default: AutoCAD 2021 put
        ATT_DVSUP of its sample at (5.278, 265.33) in its context of 1:1 alone where 1:2 was the default, its
        record keeping the default's point and given the height 6, at 1:2, of the definition 3 high (check D35)."""
    def UpdateMTextAttribute(self) -> None:
        """Places the attribute's MTEXT where its text stands, as AutoCAD's UpdateMTextAttribute, called after the
        attribute is moved or filled by DxfAttributeReference.SetAttributeFromBlock: the MTEXT's location the
        text's second point where it is not aligned left on its baseline, else its first; its height, direction,
        normal and style the text's; its attachment the text's justification, a baseline taken as the bottom; its
        words and width kept. Nothing changes for an attribute of one line, or one whose MTEXT agrees."""

class DxfBlock(System.Object):
    """A block of a DXF file as DxfReader read it: its name, its base point, its flags and its own entities in the
    block's own coordinates, as the INSERTs that place it found them."""
    @property
    def BasePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the base point of the block (groups 10, 20, 30): the point of the block an INSERT puts at its
        insertion point, scaled to millimetres where DxfReadOptions.ToMillimeters asks."""
    @property
    def Flags(self) -> int:
        """Gets the flags of the block (group 70), as the DXF reference numbers them: 1 for a block AutoCAD names
        itself, 2 for one with attributes, 4 for an external reference, 8 for one overlaid, 16 for one that
        depends on an external reference, 32 for a reference resolved; 0 for an ordinary block."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the name of the block (group 2) as its definition writes it, such as BOLT_M20, or *U12 for a block
        AutoCAD names itself."""
    @property
    def Shapes(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfShape]:
        """Gets the shapes of the entities of the block in the order of the file, in the block's own coordinates."""

class DxfBlockConnectionType(System.Enum):
    """Where the leaders of a MULTILEADER meet its block, as AutoCAD's BlockConnectionType numbers it: group 176 of
    the MULTILEADER; DxfBlockConnectionType.ConnectExtents where it gives none."""
    ConnectBase: ClassVar[DxfBlockConnectionType]
    """At the point the block is placed by, 1."""
    ConnectExtents: ClassVar[DxfBlockConnectionType]
    """At the edge of the box the block fills, 0."""
    def __init__(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    def __int__(self) -> int: ...

class DxfBlockFlipParameter(System.Object):
    """A flip parameter of a dynamic block, as DxfBlockTableRecord.AddFlipParameter wrote it: a line the block's
    entities are mirrored about, shown on every INSERT of the block as the dynamic property of its name, 0 not
    flipped and 1 flipped, and followed by the flip actions tied to it (DxfBlockTableRecord.AddFlipAction)."""
    @property
    def BasePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the reflection line starts at, in the block's coordinates."""
    @property
    def Description(self) -> str:
        """Gets the description of the property (306); empty where none was given."""
    @property
    def EndPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the reflection line runs to, in the block's coordinates."""
    @property
    def Handle(self) -> str:
        """Gets the handle of the parameter's object, the BLOCKFLIPPARAMETER of the OBJECTS section."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label of the parameter, the name of the property it gives each INSERT (305), as Hand."""

class DxfBlockLinearParameter(System.Object):
    """A linear parameter of a dynamic block, as DxfBlockTableRecord.AddLinearParameter wrote it: the distance from
    its base point to its end point, shown on every INSERT of the block as the dynamic property of its name, and
    changed by the actions tied to it (DxfBlockTableRecord.AddStretchAction, DxfBlockTableRecord.AddMoveAction,
    DxfBlockTableRecord.AddScaleAction, DxfBlockTableRecord.AddArrayAction)."""
    @property
    def BasePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the distance is measured from, in the block's coordinates, which the stretch does not
        move."""
    @property
    def Description(self) -> str:
        """Gets the description of the property (306); empty where none was given."""
    @property
    def Distance(self) -> float:
        """Gets the distance from the base point to the end point, the value every INSERT of the block shows until
        its property is set."""
    @property
    def EndPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the distance is measured to, in the block's coordinates, which follows the value set."""
    @property
    def Handle(self) -> str:
        """Gets the handle of the parameter's object, the BLOCKLINEARPARAMETER of the OBJECTS section."""
    @property
    def LabelOffset(self) -> float:
        """Gets how far the label stands off the line from the base point to the end point (140), to the left of it
        looking from the base to the end: -20 puts the label of a Width along x 20 below it."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label of the parameter, the name of the property it gives each INSERT (305), as Width."""
    @property
    def ValueSet(self) -> DxfBlockParameterValueSet:
        """Gets the values the distance may take; null where it may take any."""

class DxfBlockLookupInput(System.Object):
    """An input column of the table of a lookup parameter of a dynamic block, AutoCAD's Input Property of its Lookup
    Table: the property of another parameter that a row of the table sets, the distance of a linear parameter or
    the x or the y of a point parameter, as AutoCAD's save of ACadSharp's lookup sample holds them; the distance
    along x or along y of an XY parameter, the distance or the angle of a polar parameter, or the angle of a
    rotation parameter, as AutoCAD 2021 read and set them (plugin D25b). See
    DxfBlockTableRecord.AddLookupParameter."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Angle(parameter: DxfBlockPolarParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the angle of a polar parameter, its connection UpdatedAngle: each row gives the angle
        in radians, of the parameter's angle set where it has one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Angle(parameter: DxfBlockRotationParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the angle of a rotation parameter, its connection UpdatedAngle: each row gives the
        angle in radians from the parameter's base angle, of its value set where it has one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Distance(parameter: DxfBlockLinearParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the distance of a linear parameter, its connection UpdatedDistance as AutoCAD writes
        it: each row gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's value set where it has
        one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Distance(parameter: DxfBlockPolarParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the distance of a polar parameter, its connection UpdatedDistance as a linear
        parameter's: each row gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's distance set
        where it has one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def X(parameter: DxfBlockPointParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the x of a point parameter, its connection UpdatedX as AutoCAD writes it: each row
        gives the x."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def X(parameter: DxfBlockXYParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the distance along x of an XY parameter, its connection UpdatedDistanceX as AutoCAD's
        Civil sample writes it: each row gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's set
        along x where it has one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Y(parameter: DxfBlockPointParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the y of a point parameter, its connection UpdatedY as AutoCAD writes it: each row
        gives the y."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Y(parameter: DxfBlockXYParameter) -> DxfBlockLookupInput:
        """Makes the column of the distance along y of an XY parameter, its connection UpdatedDistanceY: each row
        gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's set along y where it has one."""

class DxfBlockLookupRow(System.Object):
    """A row of the table of a lookup parameter of a dynamic block, AutoCAD's row of its Lookup Table: the label the
    lookup property shows, and the value of each input column of the table, in the order of the columns. See
    DxfBlockTableRecord.AddLookupParameter."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, label: str, values: Sequence[float] | System.Array[float]) -> None:
        """Makes a row of a label and the values of the input columns."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, label: str, *values: float) -> None:
        """Makes a row of a label and the values of the input columns."""
    @property
    def Label(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label the lookup property shows for the row, its ends trimmed."""
    @property
    def Values(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[float]:
        """Gets the value of each input column, in the order of the columns."""

class DxfBlockParameterValueSet(System.Object):
    """The values a distance or an angle of a dynamic block's parameter may take, as AutoCAD's Block Editor sets
    them in its Value Set: from a minimum to a maximum in steps of an increment, or one of a list. A parameter
    given none takes any value. An angle's set is in radians, within a turn: Increments(0, 2 * Math.PI, Math.PI /
    12) lets an angle of 0, 15, 30 ... 360 degrees."""
    @property
    def Increment(self) -> float:
        """Gets the step of a set of increments; nought for a list."""
    @property
    def Maximum(self) -> float:
        """Gets the greatest distance of a set of increments; nought for a list."""
    @property
    def Minimum(self) -> float:
        """Gets the least distance of a set of increments; nought for a list."""
    @property
    def Values(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[float]:
        """Gets the distances of a list, from the least up; none for a set of increments."""
    @staticmethod
    def Increments(minimum: float, maximum: float, increment: float) -> DxfBlockParameterValueSet:
        """Makes a set of the distances from a minimum to a maximum in steps of an increment, as AutoCAD's Value Set
        of the type Increment: Increments(50, 300, 10) lets a Width of 50, 60 ... 300, a value between steps
        going to the nearest step and one beyond an end to that end."""
    @staticmethod
    def List(values: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[float]) -> DxfBlockParameterValueSet:
        """Makes a set of the distances listed, as AutoCAD's Value Set of the type List: List(new[] { 300.0, 50, 100
        }) lets a Width of 50, 100 or 300, a value between them going to the nearest. The list is kept from the
        least up, a value within the point tolerance of Tolerance.Default of the one before it left out. An
        angle's list may hold nought: List(new[] { 0.0, Math.PI / 2, Math.PI }) lets an arrow point along x,
        along y or back."""

class DxfBlockPointParameter(System.Object):
    """A point parameter of a dynamic block, as DxfBlockTableRecord.AddPointParameter wrote it: a position shown on
    every INSERT of the block as two dynamic properties, its label with \" X\" and \" Y\" after it, and followed
    by the move actions tied to it (DxfBlockTableRecord.AddMoveAction)."""
    @property
    def Description(self) -> str:
        """Gets the description of both properties (304); empty where none was given."""
    @property
    def Handle(self) -> str:
        """Gets the handle of the parameter's object, the BLOCKPOINTPARAMETER of the OBJECTS section."""
    @property
    def Location(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the position, in the block's coordinates, every INSERT of the block shows until its properties are
        set."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label of the parameter (303), as Tag: the properties it gives each INSERT are named Tag X and
        Tag Y."""

class DxfBlockPolarParameter(System.Object):
    """A polar parameter of a dynamic block, as DxfBlockTableRecord.AddPolarParameter wrote it: the distance from
    its base point to its end point and the angle of that line from the block's x axis, shown on every INSERT of
    the block as two dynamic properties, and followed by the polar stretch actions tied to it
    (DxfBlockTableRecord.AddPolarStretchAction), which turn and stretch with its end point, and by the stretch
    and move actions tied to it, which follow its end point unturned."""
    @property
    def Angle(self) -> float:
        """Gets the angle of the line from the base point to the end point, in radians counter-clockwise from the
        block's x axis, from nought up to 2 pi: the value every INSERT shows until its property is set."""
    @property
    def AngleDescription(self) -> str:
        """Gets the description of the angle (308); empty where none was given."""
    @property
    def AngleName(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label of the angle, the name of its property (307), as Angle."""
    @property
    def AngleValueSet(self) -> DxfBlockParameterValueSet:
        """Gets the values the angle may take, in radians; null where it may take any."""
    @property
    def BasePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the distance is measured from and the angle turns about, in the block's coordinates."""
    @property
    def Distance(self) -> float:
        """Gets the distance from the base point to the end point, the value every INSERT shows until its property
        is set."""
    @property
    def DistanceDescription(self) -> str:
        """Gets the description of the distance (306); empty where none was given."""
    @property
    def DistanceName(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label of the distance, the name of its property (305), as Length."""
    @property
    def DistanceValueSet(self) -> DxfBlockParameterValueSet:
        """Gets the values the distance may take; null where it may take any."""
    @property
    def EndPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the distance is measured to, in the block's coordinates, which follows the properties."""
    @property
    def Handle(self) -> str:
        """Gets the handle of the parameter's object, the BLOCKPOLARPARAMETER of the OBJECTS section."""
    @property
    def LabelOffset(self) -> float:
        """Gets how far the label stands off the line from the base point to the end point (140), to the left of it
        looking from the base to the end."""

class DxfBlockPropertiesTable(System.Object):
    """The block properties table of a dynamic block as the drawing keeps it, AutoCAD's BlockPropertiesTable: the
    name of the property its INSERTs show it by, the name of each column and the rows. An INSERT's property of
    that name reads the index of the row it matches and is set to one (see
    DxfDynamicBlockReferenceProperty.Value). See DxfBlockTableRecord.BlockPropertiesTable."""
    @property
    def ColumnNames(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[str]:
        """Gets the name of each column, in the order of the columns: the name of the property it sets, as Width, or
        the tag of its attribute definition."""
    @property
    def MustMatch(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block's properties must match a row, as AutoCAD's MustMatch. A distance or an angle of a
        column set then takes the INSERT to the first row that holds it beside the first row's values in the
        other columns, else, where its column holds no value twice, to the row that holds it; else it stands
        beside the first row's values and no row matches, as AutoCAD 2021 set the library's tables made to match
        (plugin D26b): of the rows 100 x 50, 200 x 80 and 150 x 60, Width 200 takes the row 1, Width 120 stands
        beside Height 50. A lookup or a user parameter of such a block, and the parameters of a table of a column
        of a user parameter or of the visibility state, are not set by the library."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the name of the property an INSERT shows the table by, Block Table1 as AutoCAD names it."""
    @property
    def Rows(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfBlockPropertiesTableRow]:
        """Gets the rows, each a value for each column: a Double (a distance in the block's units, an angle in
        radians, the real of a user parameter), a String, or null for a cell AutoCAD left empty."""

class DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn(System.Object):
    """A column of the block properties table of a dynamic block, AutoCAD's column of its Block Properties Table:
    the property of a parameter of the block that a row sets, the distance of a linear parameter, the distance
    along x or along y of an XY parameter, the distance or the angle of a polar parameter, the angle of a
    rotation parameter or the state of the visibility parameter; or an attribute definition of the block, whose
    attribute a row fills in. See DxfBlockTableRecord.AddBlockPropertiesTable."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Angle(parameter: DxfBlockPolarParameter) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the angle of a polar parameter, its connection UpdatedAngle: each row gives the angle
        in radians, of the parameter's angle set where it has one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Angle(parameter: DxfBlockRotationParameter) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the angle of a rotation parameter, its connection UpdatedAngle: each row gives the
        angle in radians from the parameter's base angle, of its value set where it has one."""
    @staticmethod
    def Attribute(definition: DxfAttributeDefinition) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of an attribute definition of the block, of no connection as AutoCAD writes it: each row
        gives the text the INSERT's attribute of its tag is given."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Distance(parameter: DxfBlockLinearParameter) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the distance of a linear parameter, its connection UpdatedDistance as AutoCAD writes
        it: each row gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's value set where it has
        one."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Distance(parameter: DxfBlockPolarParameter) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the distance of a polar parameter, its connection UpdatedDistance as a linear
        parameter's: each row gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's distance set
        where it has one."""
    @staticmethod
    def Visibility(block: DxfBlockTableRecord) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the visibility state of a block, its connection VisibilityState as AutoCAD 2021 wrote
        the column its AddItem gave a visibility parameter (plugin D26b): each row gives the name of one of the
        states, which the row shows. A block of the states Open and Closed given the rows (100, \"Open\") and
        (200, \"Closed\") of Width and this column shows Closed at the row 1."""
    @staticmethod
    def X(parameter: DxfBlockXYParameter) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the distance along x of an XY parameter, its connection UpdatedDistanceX as AutoCAD's
        Parking sample writes it: each row gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's
        set along x where it has one."""
    @staticmethod
    def Y(parameter: DxfBlockXYParameter) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn:
        """Makes the column of the distance along y of an XY parameter, its connection UpdatedDistanceY: each row
        gives the distance, above the point tolerance and of the parameter's set along y where it has one."""

class DxfBlockPropertiesTableRow(System.Object):
    """A row of the block properties table of a dynamic block, AutoCAD's row of its Block Properties Table: a value
    for each column of the table, in the order of the columns, a number for a parameter's column, the name of a
    state for the visibility's and a text, or null for an empty cell, for an attribute definition's. See
    DxfBlockTableRecord.AddBlockPropertiesTable."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, values: Sequence[object] | System.Array[object]) -> None:
        """Makes a row of a value for each column."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, *values: object) -> None:
        """Makes a row of a value for each column."""
    @property
    def Values(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[Any]:
        """Gets the value of each column, in the order of the columns: a Double or a String; null for a cell AutoCAD
        left empty in a table read from a drawing."""

class DxfBlockReference(DxfEntity):
    """An INSERT of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's BlockReference: a block placed at DxfBlockReference.Position, turned by
    DxfBlockReference.Rotation and scaled by DxfBlockReference.ScaleFactors in the plane of its
    DxfBlockReference.Normal, with the values of its attributes in DxfBlockReference.AttributeCollection."""
    def __init__(self, position: GeoPoint3, blockTableRecord: DxfBlockTableRecord) -> None:
        """Initializes an INSERT of a block at a point, as AutoCAD's new BlockReference(position, blockTableRecord):
        not turned, scaled by 1, on layer 0, in no file until it is added to a block of the drawing the block is
        of."""
    @property
    def AnonymousBlockTableRecord(self) -> DxfBlockTableRecord:
        """Gets the anonymous block that stands for the dynamic block the INSERT places, as AutoCAD's
        AnonymousBlockTableRecord: its own block where that is such a copy, *U7 of the dynamic block BOLT; null
        where it places the dynamic block itself, or no dynamic block."""
    @property
    def AttributeCollection(self) -> DxfAttributeCollection:
        """Gets the ATTRIBs of the INSERT, as AutoCAD's AttributeCollection: the values it gives its block's
        attributes, in the order of the file, read as they stand; empty where it has none. Each ATTRIB is the
        same object while its record is there; DxfAttributeCollection.AppendAttribute adds one."""
    @property
    def BlockTableRecord(self) -> DxfBlockTableRecord:
        """Gets or sets the block the INSERT places, as AutoCAD's BlockTableRecord gives its id: the record of the
        block table named by DxfBlockReference.Name; null where the drawing has no block of that name. A copy in
        no file yet, as DxfBlockReference.Explode gives a nested INSERT, places the block of the drawing it was
        copied from, as AutoCAD's copy keeps its block's id, until it is added to a drawing: a copy in no file
        gives the block of the drawing it was copied from while that block is there, renamed or not."""
    @BlockTableRecord.setter
    def BlockTableRecord(self, value: DxfBlockTableRecord) -> None: ...
    @property
    def BlockTransform(self) -> GeoTransform3:
        """Gets or sets the transformation that places the block, as AutoCAD's BlockTransform: from the coordinates
        of the block to the world, the block's origin taken to DxfBlockReference.Position, its axes scaled by
        DxfBlockReference.ScaleFactors, turned by DxfBlockReference.Rotation and stood in the plane of
        DxfBlockReference.Normal. The origin of the block is taken as (0, 0, 0) where the drawing has no block of
        the INSERT's name."""
    @BlockTransform.setter
    def BlockTransform(self, value: GeoTransform3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def BlockUnit(self) -> DxfUnits:
        """Gets the units the block is drawn in (group 70 of its BLOCK_RECORD), as AutoCAD's BlockUnit;
        DxfUnits.Undefined where the drawing gives none, as one older than R2007 does not."""
    @property
    def ClipOutline(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint2]:
        """Gets the clip boundary as a ring of points in the coordinates of the block the reference places, those
        its entities have in the block, so that DxfBlockReference.BlockTransform carries the ring to where the
        clip stands in the world: a block whose origin is (10, 20) clipped to the rectangle that, as the
        reference stands, covers its lower left corner 40 by 30 is the ring (10, 20), (50, 20), (50, 50), (10,
        50), whatever the reference is moved, turned or scaled to afterwards. A rectangle's two corners are given
        as the four of a ring. Null where the reference is not clipped; given whether the clip is on
        (DxfSpatialFilter.IsEnabled) or off. Of an external reference the ring is in the drawing's own
        coordinates, base point and all, as AutoCAD 2021 keeps it: a boundary of a drawing whose base point is
        (70, 0, 0), attached at (100, 0, 0), that stands at x 130 to 190 of the world is the ring x 100 to 160."""
    @property
    def DynamicBlockReferencePropertyCollection(
        self,
    ) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfDynamicBlockReferenceProperty]:
        """Gets the dynamic properties of the INSERT, as AutoCAD's DynamicBlockReferencePropertyCollection: a new
        list on each call, each property's value the one AutoCAD saved for this INSERT, or the dynamic block's
        own where it saved none, as for an INSERT of the dynamic block itself. Empty where the INSERT places no
        dynamic block. The value of a linear, XY, polar, point, rotation, flip, visibility, lookup, user
        parameter or block properties table property is set as AutoCAD sets it, where the block is one the
        library works out (DxfDynamicBlockReferenceProperty.Value); the others are read only."""
    @property
    def DynamicBlockTableRecord(self) -> DxfBlockTableRecord:
        """Gets the dynamic block the INSERT places, as AutoCAD's DynamicBlockTableRecord: the block whose anonymous
        copy it places, or its own block where that is the dynamic one; the INSERT's
        DxfBlockReference.BlockTableRecord where it places no dynamic block, as AutoCAD gives it."""
    @property
    def IsDynamicBlock(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the INSERT places a dynamic block, as AutoCAD's IsDynamicBlock: its block is one (its
        extension dictionary holds an evaluation graph, DxfBlockTableRecord.IsDynamicBlock), or is the anonymous
        block that stands for one, whose extended data AcDbBlockRepBTag names the dynamic block's BLOCK_RECORD by
        its handle (1005), as AutoCAD writes them and ezdxf reads them. An INSERT of a block of the extended data
        AcDbDynamicBlockGUID and no graph is not, nor one of its anonymous copy, though it keeps its
        DxfBlockReference.DynamicBlockTableRecord and DxfBlockReference.AnonymousBlockTableRecord, as AutoCAD
        2021 read the INSERTs of Bore, PVI, Station and Valve of its samples (plugin D26b). An anonymous block
        whose tag names no block of the drawing is not, nor is an INSERT scaled unlike along its axes (by more
        than 1E-9 of the largest, a mirror alike), as AutoCAD 2021 read its INSERTs scaled (2, 3, 2) and (2, 2,
        1) as not dynamic though they keep their DxfBlockReference.DynamicBlockTableRecord and their
        DxfBlockReference.DynamicBlockReferencePropertyCollection."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the name of the block the INSERT places (group 2), as AutoCAD's Name: as the block table names it,
        its escapes read as letters, such as BOLT or *U1."""
    @property
    def Normal(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets or sets the normal of the plane the INSERT turns its block in (groups 210, 220, 230), as AutoCAD's
        Normal; of unit length, (0, 0, 1) where the record gives none."""
    @Normal.setter
    def Normal(self, value: GeoVector3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Position(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets where the INSERT puts its block's origin (groups 10, 20, 30), as AutoCAD's Position: in
        world coordinates, the file's point taken from the system of the DxfBlockReference.Normal's plane; the
        origin where the record gives none. An INSERT of an annotative block stands where its context of the
        scale 1:1 says, else its default context, as AutoCAD 2021 reads one whatever CANNOSCALE says, and as
        DxfDBText.Position reads a text: the INSERT of Valve - Metric of AutoCAD's sample, its record at (13.883,
        279.776) unturned and unscaled, its context of 1:1 at (113.883, 279.776) turned 45 degrees and scaled by
        2, stands there, turned and scaled so (check D35b). Its DxfBlockReference.Rotation,
        DxfBlockReference.ScaleFactors and so DxfBlockReference.BlockTransform are that context's too."""
    @Position.setter
    def Position(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Rotation(self) -> float:
        """Gets or sets how far the INSERT turns its block (group 50, in degrees), as AutoCAD's Rotation: in
        radians, counter-clockwise about its normal; nought where the record gives none. An annotative one's is
        that of the context it is read at, as DxfBlockReference.Position says."""
    @Rotation.setter
    def Rotation(self, value: float) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ScaleFactors(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets or sets how the INSERT scales its block along its x, y and z (groups 41, 42, 43), as AutoCAD's
        ScaleFactors; 1 for each the record gives none of. A factor below nought mirrors the block. An annotative
        one's are those of the context it is read at, as DxfBlockReference.Position says."""
    @ScaleFactors.setter
    def ScaleFactors(self, value: GeoVector3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def SpatialFilter(self) -> DxfSpatialFilter:
        """Gets the clip boundary of the reference, as AutoCAD's XCLIP keeps it: the SPATIAL_FILTER under the name
        SPATIAL in the dictionary ACAD_FILTER of its extension dictionary; null where it has none, as one not
        clipped."""
    @property
    def TreatAsBlockRefForExplode(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the INSERT is exploded as a block reference, as AutoCAD's TreatAsBlockRefForExplode: true
        for every INSERT, which DxfBlockReference.Explode breaks into its block's entities; false for a MINSERT,
        of one cell or more, which it refuses, as AutoCAD 2021 gave false for its MINSERTs of 3 by 2 cells and of
        one."""
    @property
    def UnitFactor(self) -> float:
        """Gets how a length of the block is scaled to the drawing by their units, as AutoCAD's UnitFactor: the
        block's DxfBlockReference.BlockUnit against the drawing's $INSUNITS; 1 where either is
        DxfUnits.Undefined. A block drawn in inches inserted in a drawing of millimetres has 25.4; in one of
        metres, 0.0254. It is read from the file alone: the INSERT's DxfBlockReference.ScaleFactors and
        DxfBlockReference.BlockTransform do not take it in."""
    def ClipTo(self, boundary: System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint2], worldToClip: GeoTransform3) -> None:
        """Clips the block the reference places to a boundary, as AutoCAD's XCLIP New boundary does: the part of the
        block outside the boundary is no longer shown, and the part inside is. A SPATIAL_FILTER is written into
        the dictionary ACAD_FILTER of the reference's extension dictionary, each made as AutoCAD makes it, with
        the boundary as given, the matrix that carries the world into the clip coordinate system, and the inverse
        of the reference's placing as it stands now. A clip the reference has is replaced. The clip is on, with
        no clipping planes."""
    @overload
    def ConvertToStaticBlock(self) -> None:
        """Makes the INSERT of a dynamic block place an anonymous block that draws what it draws now, as AutoCAD's
        ConvertToStaticBlock(): as DxfBlockReference.ConvertToStaticBlock does, the new block named as AutoCAD
        names one itself, the first of *U1, *U2 and on the drawing has no block of and no INSERT of it names, and
        flagged anonymous (70 of 1)."""
    @overload
    def ConvertToStaticBlock(self, newBlockName: str) -> None:
        """Makes the INSERT of a dynamic block place a block of its own name that draws what it draws now, as
        AutoCAD's ConvertToStaticBlock(newBlockName): a new block of that name, its origin and units those of the
        block it places, the anonymous copy AutoCAD made for it (DxfBlockReference.AnonymousBlockTableRecord) or
        the dynamic block itself, holding copies of that block's entities, as DxfDatabase.WblockCloneObjects
        copies them; the INSERT's 2 named it, and the entry AcDbBlockRepresentation of its extension dictionary,
        which ties it to the dynamic block, taken out. The INSERT is then no dynamic block's, its attributes kept
        as they are; the anonymous block stays for the other INSERTs that place it."""
    def Explode(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfEntity]:
        """Gets the entities of the block placed where the INSERT puts them, as AutoCAD's Explode gives them: new
        entities in no file, one level down, so that an INSERT in the block comes out an INSERT, and an ATTDEF of
        the block a DxfAttributeDefinition placed as the rest are. The INSERT's ATTRIBs are not among them: their
        values stay where they are, in DxfBlockReference.AttributeCollection. A MINSERT of more than one cell is
        refused, as AutoCAD refuses one (see DxfMInsertBlock.Explode)."""
    def ExplodeToOwnerSpace(self) -> None:
        """Explodes the INSERT into the block it is in, as AutoCAD's ExplodeToOwnerSpace: the entities
        DxfBlockReference.Explode gives, an ATTDEF of the block among them, appended to the INSERT's owner, model
        space for one of model space, in the order of the block, with handles of their own. The INSERT itself is
        kept, with its ATTRIBs, as AutoCAD keeps it: insert.ExplodeToOwnerSpace(); insert.Erase(); explodes it as
        AutoCAD's EXPLODE does, the attributes turned back into their definitions. A MINSERT gives its first cell
        alone, as AutoCAD 2021's ExplodeToOwnerSpace did: its MINSERT of a circle of radius 3 in 3 columns by 2
        rows made one circle, that at the MINSERT's insertion point."""
    @overload
    def GeometryExtentsBestFit(self) -> GeoAabb3:
        """Gets the box the shapes of the block take where the INSERT places them, as AutoCAD's
        GeometryExtentsBestFit: the least and greatest x, y and z of each shape placed, not of the block's box
        placed, so that a block turned by 45 degrees has the box of its shapes, not the larger one of its turned
        box; as DxfEntity.GeometricExtents gives them."""
    @overload
    def GeometryExtentsBestFit(self, parentTransform: GeoTransform3) -> GeoAabb3:
        """Gets the box the shapes of the block take where the INSERT places them, then moved by a transformation,
        as AutoCAD's GeometryExtentsBestFit(parentTransform): the transformation that places the block the INSERT
        is in, an outer INSERT's DxfBlockReference.BlockTransform, so that an INSERT of BOLT inside FRAME has the
        box of its bolt where the INSERT of FRAME puts it. The INSERT of a block of the line from (0, 0, 0) to
        (0, 1, 0), turned by 90 degrees at (5, 0, 0), has the box (4, 0, 0) to (5, 0, 0); moved by (0, 10, 0),
        the box (4, 10, 0) to (5, 10, 0)."""
    def GetDynamicGrips(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfDynamicBlockGrip]:
        """Gets the custom grips AutoCAD shows on the INSERT of a dynamic block selected, where its values put them:
        a new list on each call, in the order of the parameters of the block's graph. Empty where the INSERT
        places no dynamic block (DxfBlockReference.IsDynamicBlock)."""
    def RemoveClip(self) -> None:
        """Takes the clip boundary off the reference, as AutoCAD's XCLIP Delete does: its SPATIAL_FILTER erased, and
        the dictionary ACAD_FILTER with it where that holds nothing else. The extension dictionary stays, as
        AutoCAD leaves it. Nothing where the reference is not clipped."""
    def ResetBlock(self) -> None:
        """Puts every dynamic property of the INSERT back to the dynamic block's own value, as AutoCAD's ResetBlock
        and its RESETBLOCK command do: the INSERT places the dynamic block itself again, and its representation
        data (the entry AcDbBlockRepresentation of its extension dictionary, with the values saved and the
        history of grip edits) is removed, the dictionary kept, as AutoCAD 2021 left it (plugin GhDyn1). The
        INSERT keeps its place, rotation, scale and ATTRIBs where they are, as AutoCAD kept the door's DOOR_NO at
        (2 800, -450) reset from a Width of 1 000 to its own 900; the anonymous block it placed is left in the
        drawing, as AutoCAD left *U2. An INSERT that places the dynamic block itself already has its
        representation data removed where it keeps some, and is left as it is where it keeps none; one that
        places no dynamic block is left as it is."""

class DxfBlockRotationParameter(System.Object):
    """A rotation parameter of a dynamic block, as DxfBlockTableRecord.AddRotationParameter wrote it: an angle about
    a base point, shown on every INSERT of the block as the dynamic property of its name, in radians, and
    followed by the rotate actions tied to it (DxfBlockTableRecord.AddRotateAction)."""
    @property
    def Angle(self) -> float:
        """Gets the angle as given, in radians counter-clockwise from the block's x axis: the angle of the grip
        about the base point, which every INSERT of the block shows, taken into a turn, until its property is
        set."""
    @property
    def BasePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point the angle turns about, in the block's coordinates."""
    @property
    def Description(self) -> str:
        """Gets the description of the property (306); empty where none was given."""
    @property
    def Handle(self) -> str:
        """Gets the handle of the parameter's object, the BLOCKROTATIONPARAMETER of the OBJECTS section."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the label of the parameter, the name of the property it gives each INSERT (305), as Angle."""
    @property
    def Radius(self) -> float:
        """Gets how far the parameter's grip stands from the base point."""
    @property
    def ValueSet(self) -> DxfBlockParameterValueSet:
        """Gets the values the angle may take, in radians; null where it may take any."""

class DxfBlockScaling(System.Enum):
    """How the INSERTs of a block may scale it, as AutoCAD's BlockScaling numbers it, group 281 of its
    BLOCK_RECORD."""
    Any: ClassVar[DxfBlockScaling]
    """By any scale along each axis, 0: what a block that gives none takes."""
    Uniform: ClassVar[DxfBlockScaling]
    """By the same scale along every axis, 1."""
    def __init__(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    def __int__(self) -> int: ...

class DxfBlockTable(DxfSymbolTable):
    """The block table of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's BlockTable: model space, paper space and every block, each a
    DxfBlockTableRecord, in the order of the file, found by name and added to."""
    def __getitem__(self, key: str) -> DxfBlockTableRecord:
        """Gets the block of a name, letters of either case the same: *Model_Space is DxfDatabase.ModelSpace."""
    def GetEnumerator(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerator[DxfBlockTableRecord]:
        """Gets an enumerator over the blocks, in the order of the file, those added after them."""
    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[DxfBlockTableRecord]: ...

class DxfBlockTableRecord(DxfSymbolTableRecord):
    """A block of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's BlockTableRecord: model space, paper space or a block; its name, its
    origin, what kind it is, and its entities, enumerated, appended to and erased."""
    ModelSpace: ClassVar[str]
    """The name AutoCAD gives the block of model space, as AutoCAD's BlockTableRecord.ModelSpace."""
    PaperSpace: ClassVar[str]
    """The name AutoCAD gives the block of paper space, as AutoCAD's BlockTableRecord.PaperSpace."""
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        """Initializes a block made in code, to be added to a DxfBlockTable with its DxfSymbolTableRecord.Name and
        DxfBlockTableRecord.Origin given."""
    @property
    def BlockPropertiesTable(self) -> DxfBlockPropertiesTable:
        """Gets the block properties table of the dynamic block, as the drawing keeps it: the name of its property,
        the name of each column and the rows (DxfBlockPropertiesTable), read anew on each call; null where the
        block has none, or one the library cannot read whole (a cell of a kind other than a real or a text)."""
    @property
    def BlockScaling(self) -> DxfBlockScaling:
        """Gets or sets how the INSERTs of the block may scale it (group 281 of its BLOCK_RECORD), as AutoCAD's
        BlockScaling; DxfBlockScaling.Any where it gives none."""
    @BlockScaling.setter
    def BlockScaling(self, value: DxfBlockScaling) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Comments(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the description of the block (group 4 of its BLOCK), as AutoCAD's Comments; empty where it
        gives none."""
    @Comments.setter
    def Comments(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Count(self) -> int:
        """Gets how many entities the block holds, a POLYLINE with its vertices one, an MTEXT with its linked
        columns one, as DxfBlockTableRecord.GetEnumerator walks them."""
    @property
    def DrawOrderTable(self) -> DxfDrawOrderTable:
        """Gets the draw order of the block, as AutoCAD's DrawOrderTableId names it: the SORTENTSTABLE under
        ACAD_SORTENTS in the block's extension dictionary; null where the block has none, its entities then drawn
        in the order of the block."""
    @property
    def Explodable(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the INSERTs of the block may be exploded (group 280 of its BLOCK_RECORD), as
        AutoCAD's Explodable; true where it gives none."""
    @Explodable.setter
    def Explodable(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def HasAttributeDefinitions(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block has attribute definitions (flag 2), as AutoCAD's HasAttributeDefinitions: set when
        one is appended (DxfBlockTableRecord.AppendEntity), constant or not, in model space too, and kept when it
        is erased, as AutoCAD 2021 sets and saves it; a block read from a file says what its file says."""
    @property
    def HasPreviewIcon(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block has a preview picture (groups 310 of its BLOCK_RECORD), as AutoCAD's
        HasPreviewIcon."""
    @property
    def Hyperlinks(self) -> DxfHyperLinkCollection:
        """Gets the hyperlinks of the block, as AutoCAD's Hyperlinks: those of the extended data of the application
        PE_URL of its BLOCK_RECORD, as DxfHyperLinkCollection says."""
    @property
    def IsAnonymous(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block is one AutoCAD names itself, as a dimension's *D1 (flag 1 of its BLOCK's group
        70), as AutoCAD's IsAnonymous: true of a block added named *D, *U or *T, which the table names *D1, *U1
        or *T1 and on."""
    @property
    def IsDynamicBlock(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block is a dynamic block, as AutoCAD's IsDynamicBlock: its extension dictionary holds
        the evaluation graph of its parameters and actions (the entry ACAD_ENHANCEDBLOCK). The extended data
        AcDbDynamicBlockGUID does not make it one: AutoCAD 2021 read the Bore, PVI, Station and Valve blocks of
        its Dynamic Blocks samples, which keep the GUID over an empty extension dictionary, as not dynamic, and a
        block whose GUID was taken out and its graph kept as dynamic (plugin D26b)."""
    @property
    def IsFromExternalReference(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block is an external reference (flag 4), as AutoCAD's IsFromExternalReference."""
    @property
    def IsFromOverlayReference(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block is an external reference overlaid (flag 8), as AutoCAD's
        IsFromOverlayReference."""
    @property
    def IsLayout(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the block is that of a layout, as AutoCAD's IsLayout: model space, paper space, or the block
        of another layout, *Paper_Space0 and on, or one whose BLOCK_RECORD names a layout (group 340)."""
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the name of the block, as DxfSymbolTableRecord.Name: AutoCAD's *Model_Space and *Paper_Space
        for model space and paper space, whatever the file calls them, as a file of R12 calls them $Model_Space
        and $Paper_Space."""
    @Name.setter
    def Name(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Origin(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets the origin of the block (groups 10, 20, 30 of its BLOCK), as AutoCAD's Origin: the point of
        the block an INSERT puts at its insertion point; the origin of the world for model and paper space."""
    @Origin.setter
    def Origin(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def PathName(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the path of the drawing an external reference comes from (group 1 of its BLOCK), as
        AutoCAD's PathName; empty for a block that is none."""
    @PathName.setter
    def PathName(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @property
    def PreviewIcon(self) -> System.Array[int]:
        """Gets or sets the preview picture of the block, as AutoCAD's PreviewIcon gives it as a bitmap: here the
        bytes its BLOCK_RECORD keeps, the groups 310 one after another, a bitmap of Windows without the file's
        header, as AutoCAD writes it; null where it has none."""
    @PreviewIcon.setter
    def PreviewIcon(self, value: Sequence[int] | System.Array[int] | None) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Units(self) -> DxfUnits:
        """Gets or sets the unit the block is drawn in (group 70 of its BLOCK_RECORD), as AutoCAD's Units: an INSERT
        of a block in millimetres into a drawing in metres scales it by a thousandth; DxfUnits.Undefined where it
        gives none."""
    @Units.setter
    def Units(self, value: DxfUnits) -> None: ...
    @property
    def XrefStatus(self) -> DxfXrefStatus:
        """Gets where the external reference stands, as AutoCAD's XrefStatus, from its BLOCK's flags and its path:
        DxfXrefStatus.NotAnXref for a block that is none (flag 4 clear); DxfXrefStatus.Unreferenced where no
        INSERT places it; DxfXrefStatus.FileNotFound where its DxfBlockTableRecord.PathName is no file, as
        written or from the folder of the drawing's DxfDatabase.Filename; DxfXrefStatus.Resolved where AutoCAD
        saved it resolved (flag 32); DxfXrefStatus.Unresolved otherwise, as one attached here stands until
        AutoCAD opens the drawing and resolves it. DxfXrefStatus.Unloaded is never given: no group of a DXF file
        says an external reference is unloaded."""
    def AddAlignmentParameter(self, basePoint: GeoPoint3, endPoint: GeoPoint3) -> None:
        """Makes the block dynamic, where it is not, and gives it an alignment parameter, AutoCAD's Alignment
        parameter as its Block Editor makes one: a grip at the base point that turns an INSERT dragged by it in
        AutoCAD to lie along the entity it is dragged over, along the line from the base point to the end point.
        It gives no property."""
    @overload
    def AddArrayAction(
        self,
        parameter: DxfBlockLinearParameter,
        entities: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfEntity],
        columnSpacing: float,
    ) -> None:
        """Gives the block an array action tied to a linear parameter of it, AutoCAD's Array action as its Block
        Editor makes one: as the parameter's distance grows, the entities are copied along the line from the
        parameter's base point to its end point, a copy at each column spacing, as many in all as the spacing
        goes whole into the distance."""
    @overload
    def AddArrayAction(
        self,
        parameter: DxfBlockXYParameter,
        entities: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfEntity],
        columnSpacing: float,
        rowSpacing: float,
    ) -> None:
        """Gives the block an array action tied to an XY parameter of it, AutoCAD's Array action as its Block Editor
        makes one: as the parameter's end point moves, the entities are copied in rows and columns from the base
        point the way the end point lies, a column at each column spacing along x and a row at each row spacing
        along y."""
    def AddBasePointParameter(self, location: GeoPoint3) -> None:
        """Makes the block dynamic, where it is not, and gives it a base point parameter, AutoCAD's Base Point
        parameter as its Block Editor makes one: a base point for the INSERTs of the block apart from its origin.
        It gives no property."""
    def AddBlockPropertiesTable(
        self,
        location: GeoPoint3,
        columns: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfBlockPropertiesTableColumn],
        rows: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfBlockPropertiesTableRow],
    ) -> None:
        """Makes the block dynamic, where it is not, and gives it a block properties table: rows of values, each
        setting several properties of the block's parameters and attributes at once, which each INSERT of the
        block shows as the dynamic property Block Table1, the index of its row, AutoCAD's Block Properties Table
