    def FormatMeasurement(self, measurement: float, dimensionText: str) -> str:
        """Gets the text the dimension writes for a measurement, as AutoCAD's FormatMeasurement: the measurement in
        the units and to the places of the variables it reads, put into a text as its own text is. A length is
        multiplied by DxfDimension.Dimlfac (a negative one taken as its size in paper space and as 1 elsewhere,
        as AutoCAD takes it), rounded by DxfDimension.Dimrnd and written in DxfDimension.Dimlunit: 1 scientific,
        2 decimal, 3 engineering, 4 architectural, 5 fractional, 6 as the Windows desktop writes it under the
        culture of the thread; to DxfDimension.Dimdec places, or in architectural and fractional units to a
        fraction of 2 to the power of them, stacked as DxfDimension.Dimfrac says in AutoCAD's codes of an MTEXT;
        its zeros left out as DxfDimension.Dimzin says, DxfDimension.Dimdsep its decimal separator,
        DxfDimension.Dimpost about it; and where DxfDimension.Dimalt is on, its alternate units after it in
        brackets, or in the place of a [] of the text. An angle, of a DxfLineAngularDimension2 or a
        DxfPoint3AngularDimension, is given in radians and written in DxfDimension.Dimaunit (0 decimal degrees, 1
        degrees, minutes and seconds, 2 grads, 3 radians) to DxfDimension.Dimadec places (those of
        DxfDimension.Dimdec at -1), its zeros left out as DxfDimension.Dimazin says. In the style ISO-25, two
        places, a comma and trailing zeros left out, 1234.5 is 1234,5 and 60 is 60; in architectural units to a
        sixteenth, not stacked, 15.5 is 1'-3 1/2\"; to two decimal places 2.675 is 2.68, a number being rounded
        as its 15 significant figures (a .NET decimal), half away from nought; pi / 4 of an angular dimension is
        45°. Tolerances, limits, the arc symbol and the R or diameter sign before a radius are not part of it."""
    def GetDimstyleData(self) -> DxfDimStyleTableRecord:
        """Gets the variables the dimension is drawn with, as AutoCAD's GetDimstyleData: a new
        DxfDimStyleTableRecord in no table, named as the dimension's style, each variable as the dimension reads
        it, its override or its style's."""
    def ReleaseDimAssoc(self) -> None:
        """Unties the dimension from the objects its points were tied to, as AutoCAD disassociates it
        (DIMDISASSOCIATE, or the last object it was tied to erased): the DIMASSOC taken out of the reactors of
        each object and of the dimension and erased, and the extension dictionary released where it is left
        empty, as AutoCAD leaves a dimension with none. The dimension keeps its points and its picture. Nothing
        for a dimension tied to nothing."""
    def RemoveTextField(self) -> None:
        """Takes out the field of the dimension's text, as AutoCAD's RemoveTextField: as DxfDBObject.RemoveField
        takes it out, with its children, the text the dimension writes (1) kept. Nothing where it has none."""
    def SetDimAssoc(self, references: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfOsnapPointRef]) -> DxfDimAssoc:
        """Ties the dimension's points to objects, as AutoCAD 2021 ties a dimension made with DIMASSOC 2 by object
        snaps: a DIMASSOC under ACAD_DIMASSOC in the dimension's extension dictionary (made where it has none),
        owned by the dictionary, naming the dimension and each reference, and listed among the reactors of the
        dimension and of every object it names; the class DIMASSOC listed. A dimension tied already has its
        DIMASSOC written anew, the same handle, an object it no longer names losing the reactor. A DIMLINEAR from
        the start of the line 2A to its end is tied by dimension.SetDimAssoc(new[] { new DxfOsnapPointRef(0,
        DxfOsnapType.StartPoint, \"2A\", 0, 0, start, null), new DxfOsnapPointRef(1, DxfOsnapType.Endpoint,
        \"2A\", 0, 1, end, null) }). The dimension's points are not moved: they are where the references say
        already."""
    def SetDimstyleData(self, style: DxfDimStyleTableRecord) -> None:
        """Gives the dimension the variables of a record, as AutoCAD's SetDimstyleData: each that differs from what
        the dimension reads written as an override, as its setter writes one; those the dimension reads already
        change nothing. A variable its file's version has not is passed over where the record holds AutoCAD's own
        value of it, and refused where it holds another; a record that names no text style leaves the dimension's
        as it is. A whole number is checked against AutoCAD's range as DxfDatabase.SetDimstyleData checks it, a
        Dimdec of 9 refused, and a size of the arrows, the text or the scale below nought. Every value is checked
        before any is written."""
    def SetFromStyle(self) -> bool:
        """Takes away the dimension's overrides of its dimension style, as AutoCAD's SetFromStyle: the list DSTYLE
        of its extended data of ACAD, the rest of that data kept, and the data of ACAD with it where nothing else
        is left; each variable then reads as its style has it, a dimension of Dimasz 4.5 of its own over a style
        of 3.5 reading 3.5. A dimension of no overrides changes nothing. The block AutoCAD drew the dimension
        with is not drawn anew."""

