        underlays (DxfPdfDefinition.CreatePdfDictionary)."""
    @property
    def ItemName(self) -> str:
        """Gets the name of the page (group 2), as AutoCAD's ItemName: the number of the page as text for a PDF, 1
        for the first; empty where the record gives none."""
    @property
    def SourceFileName(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the path of the PDF file (group 1), as AutoCAD's SourceFileName: as the file writes it, a
        path of the machine it was drawn on or one relative to the drawing."""
    @SourceFileName.setter
    def SourceFileName(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @staticmethod
    def CreatePdfDictionary(database: DxfDatabase) -> DxfDBDictionary:
        """Gets the dictionary of the PDF underlays of a drawing, made where it has none: ACAD_PDFUNDERLAYS of the
        named object dictionary, owned by it, of entries kept (281 of 1), as AutoCAD 2021 writes it."""
    def Erase(self) -> None:
        """Erases the definition, as AutoCAD 2021's Erase of a PdfDefinition: its entry of the dictionary of PDF
        underlays taken out, and with it every underlay of the drawing that shows it."""
    def GetEntityCount(self) -> int:
        """Gets how many underlays of the drawing show the definition: those whose handle (340) it is, an underlay
        in a block as one in model space; an erased underlay is not counted."""
    @staticmethod
    def GetPdfDictionary(database: DxfDatabase) -> DxfDBDictionary:
        """Gets the dictionary of the PDF underlays of a drawing: ACAD_PDFUNDERLAYS of the named object dictionary,
        each DxfPdfDefinition under its name; null where the drawing has none."""
    @staticmethod
    def SuggestName(pdfDictionary: DxfDBDictionary, path: str, itemName: str) -> str:
        """Gives a name for a definition of a page in a dictionary of PDF underlays, as the External References
        palette names one: the file's name without its folder or extension, then - Page_ and the page, sample -
        Page_1 for page 1 of C:\\plans\\sample.pdf; where the dictionary has that name, letters of either case
        the same, the name and _1, or _2 and on, the first it has not."""
    def ToString(self) -> str:
        """Gives the definition as a line for debugging: its type, its handle, its path and its page."""

class DxfPdfUnderlay(DxfEntity):
    """A PDFUNDERLAY of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's PdfReference: one page of a PDF file placed in the drawing, its
    file and page named by its PDFDEFINITION (DxfPdfUnderlay.Definition), shown at a place, a scale and a turn,
    faded, in grey or clipped as its record says. The library reads no PDF: it places, scales and clips the
    underlay as its record says."""
    def __init__(self, definition: DxfPdfDefinition) -> None:
        """Initializes an underlay made in code of a definition of a drawing, as AutoCAD's new PdfReference() given
        its DefinitionId: its corner at the origin, scale 1 along every side, not turned, shown, its colours
        adjusted, its contrast 100 and its fade 0, with no clip boundary, as AutoCAD 2021 writes a new one.
        Appended to a block of the definition's drawing by DxfBlockTableRecord.AppendEntity, it is counted by
        DxfPdfDefinition.GetEntityCount."""
    @property
    def AdjustColorForBackground(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the colours are adjusted for the background, as AutoCAD's AdjustColorForBackground
        (flag 8); true as it is made."""
    @AdjustColorForBackground.setter
    def AdjustColorForBackground(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Contrast(self) -> int:
        """Gets or sets the contrast (group 281), as AutoCAD's Contrast: 0 to 100, 100 as it is made, where the
        colours are as the PDF has them."""
    @Contrast.setter
    def Contrast(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Definition(self) -> DxfPdfDefinition:
        """Gets the definition the underlay shows (group 340), as AutoCAD's DefinitionId names it: of its drawing,
        of the drawing it was copied from for a copy in no file; null where the drawing has no PDFDEFINITION of
        the handle."""
    @property
    def Fade(self) -> int:
        """Gets or sets the fade (group 282), as AutoCAD's Fade: 0 to 100, 0 as it is made, where the colours are as
        the PDF has them; 100 fades them into the background."""
    @Fade.setter
    def Fade(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    @property
    def HasClipBoundary(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the underlay has a clip boundary, two corners or a polygon (the run of 11 with its 21),
        whether or not it is on (DxfPdfUnderlay.IsClipped)."""
    @property
    def IsClipInverted(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the underlay shows what lies outside its boundary and hides what lies inside, as
        AutoCAD's IsClipInverted (flag 16); false as it is made."""
    @IsClipInverted.setter
    def IsClipInverted(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def IsClipped(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the underlay is clipped, as AutoCAD's IsClipped (flag 1): true as it is made, which
        clips nothing while the underlay has no boundary (DxfPdfUnderlay.HasClipBoundary), as AutoCAD 2021 keeps
        a new one."""
    @IsClipped.setter
    def IsClipped(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def IsOn(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the underlay is shown, as AutoCAD's IsOn (flag 2 of group 280); true as it is
        made."""
    @IsOn.setter
    def IsOn(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Monochrome(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the underlay is shown in monochrome, as AutoCAD's Monochrome (flag 4); false as it
        is made."""
    @Monochrome.setter
    def Monochrome(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets the name of the underlay, as AutoCAD's Name: the name its PDFDEFINITION has in the dictionary of PDF
        underlays (ACAD_PDFUNDERLAYS), such as sample - Page_1; null where it shows no definition of the
        dictionary."""
    @property
    def NameOfSheet(self) -> str:
        """Gets the name of the page, as AutoCAD's NameOfSheet: the number of the page as text, 1 for the first;
        empty where it shows none."""
    @property
    def Normal(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets or sets the normal of the plane the underlay lies in, as AutoCAD's Normal (groups 210, 220, 230):
        (0, 0, 1) for one laid in the plane xy, as it is made."""
    @Normal.setter
    def Normal(self, value: GeoVector3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Path(self) -> str:
        """Gets the path of the PDF file, as AutoCAD's Path: the path its definition names, as the file writes it;
        empty where it shows none."""
    @property
    def Position(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets the corner of the page, as AutoCAD's Position: where the lower left corner of the page
        stands, in world coordinates (groups 10, 20, 30)."""
    @Position.setter
    def Position(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Rotation(self) -> float:
        """Gets or sets the turn of the underlay about its corner, as AutoCAD's Rotation, in radians in the plane of
        the DxfPdfUnderlay.Normal; the file writes degrees (group 50): 0.5 radian is 28.6479."""
    @Rotation.setter
    def Rotation(self, value: float) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ScaleFactors(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets or sets the scale along the page's width, its height and its depth, as AutoCAD's ScaleFactors
        (groups 41, 42, 43): 1 for every side as it is made. The page 2.7778 by 1.3889 inches given the scale
        (25.4, 25.4, 25.4) is 70.56 by 35.28."""
    @ScaleFactors.setter
    def ScaleFactors(self, value: GeoVector3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Transform(self) -> GeoTransform3:
        """Gets the transformation from the page's inches to the world, as AutoCAD's Transform: the page's (x, y),
        from its lower left corner, scaled, turned in the plane of the normal and moved to the corner. The page
        2.7778 inches wide at the scale 2 at (10, 20) takes (1, 0) to (12, 20, 0); turned a quarter turn, to (10,
        22, 0)."""
    def ClearClipBoundary(self) -> None:
        """Takes the clip boundary away, as AutoCAD's PDFCLIP Delete: the whole page is shown, the clip on as a new
        underlay has it."""
    def GetClipBoundary(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint2]:
        """Gets the clip boundary, as AutoCAD's GetClipBoundary: in the page's inches from its lower left corner,
        before the scale. Two corners for a rectangle, as AutoCAD stores it, the upper left and the lower right;
        the corners of a polygon otherwise, not repeating the first at the end; none for an underlay with no
        boundary."""
    def GetClipFrame(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint3]:
        """Gets the clip boundary as a closed polygon in world coordinates, as AutoCAD's frame draws it: the
        rectangle's four corners or the polygon's, laid through DxfPdfUnderlay.Transform; none for an underlay
        with no boundary."""
    def SetClipBoundary(self, corners: System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint2]) -> None:
        """Sets the clip boundary, as AutoCAD's SetClipBoundary, and switches the clip on: two corners are a
        rectangle, written as AutoCAD 2021 writes it, the upper left and the lower right, so that (1, 1) and (2,
        2) are (1, 2) and (2, 1); three or more are a polygon, written as given. The page's inches from its lower
        left corner, before the scale."""
    def SetDefinition(self, definition: DxfPdfDefinition) -> None:
        """Makes the underlay show another definition of its drawing, as AutoCAD's DefinitionId set: its 340 the
        definition's handle, the definition's reactors given the underlay."""

