        through it and its neighbours. Where the tangents at a segment's ends are either side of it, its arcs
        meet where the curve runs along the chord; where they are on one side (an S), the arcs' radii are as the
        sines of the tangents' angles to the chord. A segment whose tangent at either end is within a millionth
        of a radian of its line stays straight, with no vertex added, as do the two vertices of a polyline of
        two; and two vertices on one point split the curve in two there. Every vertex and bulge is AutoCAD 2021's
        to 1E-11. A segment's widths run along its two arcs, the width at the joint read off at the first arc's
        share of their length, as AutoCAD reads it: a segment from width 1 to 3 whose first arc is 25.723 long
        and second 24.733 is 2.0197 wide at the joint. A fitted polyline is straightened first. Each vertex of
        the frame keeps its handle."""
