        DxfPolyline2d.SplineFit fits it."""
    @overload
    def SplineFit(self, value: DxfPoly2dType, segments: int) -> None:
        """Fits the polyline with a spline, as AutoCAD's SplineFit: its vertices made the frame of a uniform
        B-spline (flag 16 of their group 70, each keeping its handle), clamped to the first and last vertex of an
        open polyline and running round a closed one, and the vertices of the curve added after the first of them
        (flag 8), where AutoCAD keeps them, a number of segments to each span of the spline; flag 4 of the
        polyline's group 70 and group 75, 5 or 6. A negative number of segments gives as many, each the arc
        through its ends and the spline's point between them, as AutoCAD's SPLINESEGS below nought fits arcs to
        them. The widths run evenly from the first vertex's start width to the last's end width. A cubic on the
        frame (0, 0), (10, 10), (20, 0) is of degree 2 on its three points, one span drawn through (0, 0) and
        (20, 0) with (10, 5) at its middle, in 8 segments where SPLINESEGS is 8; on the frame (0, 0), (10, 10),
        (20, 0), (30, 10) it is a cubic of one span too. A fitted polyline is straightened first."""
    def Straighten(self) -> None:
        """Straightens a polyline fitted with a curve or a spline, as AutoCAD's Straighten: the vertices the fitting
        made (flags 1 and 8) are taken out, those of the frame (16) are vertices of the polyline again, and flags
