        drawing it was copied from for a copy in no file; null for a WIPEOUT, which shows none, and where the
        drawing has no IMAGEDEF of the handle."""
    @property
    def ImageHeight(self) -> float:
        """Gets how many pixels the image is up (group 23), as AutoCAD's ImageHeight: 3 for a picture of 4 by 3; one
        for a WIPEOUT."""
    @property
    def ImageTransparency(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the transparent pixels of the image are shown as such (flag 8 of group 70), as
        AutoCAD's ImageTransparency."""
    @ImageTransparency.setter
    def ImageTransparency(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ImageWidth(self) -> float:
        """Gets how many pixels the image is across (group 13), as AutoCAD's ImageWidth: 4 for a picture of 4 by 3;
        one for a WIPEOUT."""
    @property
    def IsClipInverted(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the boundary keeps the image outside it rather than inside (group 290), as
        ObjectARX's isClipInverted, which AutoCAD 2021's .NET API does not give; false where the record gives
        none, as in every file before R2010. The boundary, its vertices and the lines it explodes into stay as
        they are."""
    @IsClipInverted.setter
    def IsClipInverted(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def IsClipped(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the image is clipped by its boundary, as AutoCAD 2021's IsClipped reads and sets it:
        flag 4 of group 70, which AutoCAD sets on every new image. The boundary clips it where its record also
        says one was set (280 of 1, which DxfRasterImage.SetClipBoundary writes): the image clipped by a triangle
        and given false keeps its triangle, and shows its whole frame again, its 280 left at 1, as AutoCAD 2021
        leaves it."""
    @IsClipped.setter
    def IsClipped(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Name(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the name of the image, as AutoCAD's Name: the name its IMAGEDEF has in the dictionary of
        images (ACAD_IMAGE_DICT), such as px43; null where it shows no IMAGEDEF or none of the dictionary, as a
        WIPEOUT, for which AutoCAD 2021 throws."""
    @Name.setter
    def Name(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Path(self) -> str:
        """Gets the file of the picture, as AutoCAD's Path: the path its IMAGEDEF names (group 1), as the file
        writes it; null where it shows none, as a WIPEOUT, for which AutoCAD 2021 throws."""
    @property
    def PixelToModelTransform(self) -> GeoTransform3:
        """Gets the transformation from the pixels of the image to the world, as AutoCAD 2021's
        PixelToModelTransform: the pixel (x, y), counted from the centre of the top left pixel with y down, to
        its place, the third axis the image's normal. The picture of 4 by 3 pixels 10 apart placed at (10, 20)
        takes the pixel (0, 0) to (15, 45, 0) and (-0.5, -0.5), the top left corner, to (10, 50, 0)."""
    @property
    def Position(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the corner of the image opposite the one it is placed at, as AutoCAD 2021's Position gives it: the
        placing corner (10) and the image's width and height along its pixels. The image 40 by 30 placed at (10,
        20) gives (50, 50); the corner it is placed at is the origin of DxfRasterImage.GetOrientation."""
    @property
    def Rotation(self) -> float:
        """Gets or sets the angle of the bottom of the image in the world's plane xy, as AutoCAD 2021's Rotation:
        from the x axis, counter-clockwise, from 0 to 2 pi, of the vector of one pixel across seen from above; 0
        for an image placed along x, pi for one mirrored about the y axis."""
    @Rotation.setter
    def Rotation(self, value: float) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ShowImage(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the image is shown (flag 1 of group 70), as AutoCAD's ShowImage; set, written as
        DxfRasterImage.DisplayOptions writes it."""
    @ShowImage.setter
    def ShowImage(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Width(self) -> float:
        """Gets the length of the bottom of the image (the side u of DxfRasterImage.GetOrientation), as AutoCAD's
        Width: 40 for 4 pixels 10 across."""
    def AssociateRasterDef(self, definition: DxfRasterImageDef) -> None:
        """Makes the image show a definition of its drawing, as AutoCAD's AssociateRasterDef: its 340 the
        definition, its size in pixels the definition's, its sides kept, so that the picture 40 by 30 of 4 by 3
        pixels given one of 8 by 6 stays 40 by 30 of 8 by 6, its boundary scaled with the pixels, a polygon
        another writer left not closed written closed, as AutoCAD 2021 cannot open a drawing of an image whose
        polygon is not; and its IMAGEDEF_REACTOR taken from the definition it showed to this one, or made, as
        AutoCAD 2021 makes one, so that DxfRasterImageDef.GetEntityCount counts it."""
    def Explode(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfEntity]:
        """Gets the lines the image breaks into, as AutoCAD 2021's Explode breaks an IMAGE and a WIPEOUT: a LINE
        along each side of DxfRasterImage.GetVertices, the frame of the image not clipped and its boundary
        clipped, each with the image's look, a side of no length left out. The picture 40 by 30 placed at (10,
        20) gives four LINEs, from (10, 20, 0) to (10, 50, 0) and round; clipped by a triangle, three. AutoCAD's
        lines have no look of their own, to take the drawing's when appended."""
    def GetClipBoundary(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint2]:
        """Gets the clip boundary of the image in pixels, as AutoCAD 2021's GetClipBoundary gives it read from a
        file: a rectangle of the two corners its record holds as its five corners, the first again at the end,
        from its least corner, (x, y) of the least of each, up its x to the greatest y and round, whichever way
        the two are held; a polygon as its record holds it. The picture of 4 by 3 pixels not clipped holds (-0.5,
        -0.5) and (3.5, 2.5), and gives (-0.5, -0.5), (-0.5, 2.5), (3.5, 2.5), (3.5, -0.5), (-0.5, -0.5). The
        pixels are counted from the centre of the top left one, y down; a WIPEOUT's from -0.5 to 0.5 of its
        frame."""
    def GetOrientation(self) -> tuple[GeoPoint3, GeoVector3, GeoVector3]:
        """Gives the corner the image is placed at and its two sides, as AutoCAD's Orientation gives them: the
        corner (group 10), the side along the bottom, the vector of one pixel across (11) times the pixels across
        (13), and the side up the left, the vector of one pixel up (12) times the pixels up (23). The image of 4
        by 3 pixels 10 apart placed at (10, 20) gives (10, 20, 0), (40, 0, 0) and (0, 30, 0). The sides keep
        their lengths, and need not be square: AutoCAD keeps a sheared image so."""
    def GetVertices(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint3]:
        """Gets the corners of the image as it is shown, in world coordinates, the first again at the end, as
        AutoCAD 2021's GetVertices gives them. Clipped (DxfRasterImage.IsClipped, and a boundary set, 280 of 1),
        the corners of its boundary taken to the world (DxfRasterImage.PixelToModelTransform): a rectangle from
        its least corner, (x, y) of the least of each, up its x to the greatest y and on; a polygon in its order.
        Else the frame of the whole image, from the corner it is placed at up its left side and round: the
        picture 40 by 30 placed at (10, 20) gives (10, 20, 0), (10, 50, 0), (50, 50, 0), (50, 20, 0) and (10, 20,
        0); clipped by the triangle of the pixels (0, 0), (3, 0), (1.5, 2.5), it gives (15, 45, 0), (45, 45, 0),
        (30, 20, 0) and (15, 45, 0)."""
    def ImageSize(self, getCachedValue: bool) -> GeoVector2:
        """Gets the size of the image in pixels, as AutoCAD's ImageSize: the size its record keeps (13, 23), or, not
        cached, the size its IMAGEDEF gives (10, 20), the record's where it has none. The library reads no image
        file: what AutoCAD reads of the file when it loads it is the size its IMAGEDEF was given."""
    def SetClipBoundary(
        self,
        type: DxfClipBoundaryType,
        clipBoundaryVertices: System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[GeoPoint2],
    ) -> None:
        """Clips the image by a boundary, as AutoCAD's SetClipBoundary: a rectangle given by its five corners, the
        first again at the end, written as the first and the third, as AutoCAD 2021 writes it; a polygon of three
        corners or more, its first again at the end, written as given, the last as the first. The boundary is in
        pixels, counted from the centre of the top left pixel with y down, and may cross itself or leave the
        image, as AutoCAD takes it; its record is said to be clipped (280 of 1). DxfRasterImage.IsClipped is left
        as it is: the image clips by the boundary where it is on, as AutoCAD sets it on every new image."""
    def SetClipBoundaryToWholeImage(self) -> None:
        """Clips the image by nothing, as AutoCAD's SetClipBoundaryToWholeImage: its boundary the rectangle of the
        whole image, from (-0.5, -0.5) to the pixels across and up less a half, (3.5, 2.5) for a picture of 4 by
        3 and (0.5, 0.5) for a WIPEOUT, and its record said to be clipped by none (280 of 0), as AutoCAD 2021
        writes it."""
    def SetOrientation(self, origin: GeoPoint3, u: GeoVector3, v: GeoVector3) -> None:
        """Places the image anew, as AutoCAD's Orientation set: at a corner with its two sides, written as the
        vectors of one pixel (11 and 12), each side divided by the pixels along it; the clip boundary, in pixels,
        goes with the image. The image of 4 by 3 pixels set at (0, 0, 0) with the sides (80, 0, 0) and (0, 60, 0)
        has pixels 20 across and 20 up. The sides need not be square or of one scale, as AutoCAD 2021 takes them."""

class DxfRasterImageDef(DxfDBObject):
    """An IMAGEDEF of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's RasterImageDef: the picture file the IMAGEs of a drawing show, under
    its name in the dictionary of images (DxfRasterImageDef.GetImageDictionary), with the size in pixels and the
    size of a pixel AutoCAD read from the file when it loaded it."""
    def __init__(self, sourceFileName: str, size: GeoVector2) -> None:
        """Initializes a definition made in code of a picture file, as AutoCAD's new RasterImageDef() given its
        SourceFileName and loaded: the path as it is to be written, and the size in pixels the caller gives,
        which AutoCAD reads from the file when it loads it and the library does not; a pixel (1, 1) in no unit,
        and loaded (280 of 1), as ezdxf writes a new one, so that AutoCAD loads the picture when it opens the
        drawing. Added to a drawing by DxfDBDictionary.SetAt of its dictionary of images
        (DxfRasterImageDef.CreateImageDictionary)."""
    @property
    def IsLoaded(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether AutoCAD had the picture loaded when it saved the drawing (group 280), as AutoCAD's IsLoaded
        was then; true where the record gives none, and for a definition made in code."""
    @property
    def ResolutionMMPerPixel(self) -> GeoVector2:
        """Gets or sets the size of one pixel in millimetres (groups 11, 21), as AutoCAD's ResolutionMMPerPixel:
        (0.2646, 0.2646) for a picture of 96 dots an inch; (1, 1) where the record gives none, as ezdxf and
        ACadSharp read none, and for a definition made in code."""
    @ResolutionMMPerPixel.setter
    def ResolutionMMPerPixel(self, value: GeoVector2) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ResolutionUnits(self) -> DxfUnit:
        """Gets or sets the unit the picture's resolution is given in (group 281), as AutoCAD's ResolutionUnits:
        centimetres (2) or inches (5) for a picture that says its resolution, none (0) for one that does not."""
    @ResolutionUnits.setter
    def ResolutionUnits(self, value: DxfUnit) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Size(self) -> GeoVector2:
        """Gets the size of the picture in pixels (groups 10, 20), as AutoCAD's Size: (4, 3) for a picture of 4 by
        3; (0, 0) where the record gives none."""
    @property
    def SourceFileName(self) -> str:
        """Gets or sets the path of the picture file (group 1), as AutoCAD's SourceFileName: as the file writes it,
        a path of the machine it was drawn on or one relative to the drawing, such as C:\\pictures\\px43.png."""
    @SourceFileName.setter
    def SourceFileName(self, value: str) -> None: ...
    @staticmethod
    def CreateImageDictionary(database: DxfDatabase) -> DxfDBDictionary:
        """Gets the dictionary of the images of a drawing, made where it has none, as AutoCAD's
        CreateImageDictionary makes it: ACAD_IMAGE_DICT of the named object dictionary, owned by it, of entries
        kept (281 of 1). The one the drawing has where it has one, where AutoCAD 2021 makes a new one in its
        place and erases the old with its definitions."""
    def Erase(self) -> None:
        """Erases the definition, as AutoCAD 2021's Erase of a RasterImageDef: its entry of the dictionary of images
        taken out, and with it every image of the drawing that shows it, as AutoCAD takes those associated with
        it. AutoCAD leaves an image of no reactor pointing at the definition erased, which the library does not:
        a copy is erased with the rest."""
    def GetEntityCount(self) -> tuple[int, bool]:
        """Gets how many images of the drawing are associated with the definition, as AutoCAD 2021's GetEntityCount
        counts them: those whose IMAGEDEF_REACTOR the definition lists, an image made in code and appended, or
        associated by DxfRasterImage.AssociateRasterDef; a copy, which AutoCAD's Clone appended leaves with no
        reactor, is not counted, as AutoCAD counts it not. Two images in a block placed by two INSERTs count once
        each."""
    @staticmethod
    def GetImageDictionary(database: DxfDatabase) -> DxfDBDictionary:
        """Gets the dictionary of the images of a drawing, as AutoCAD's GetImageDictionary gives its id:
        ACAD_IMAGE_DICT of the named object dictionary, each DxfRasterImageDef under its name; null where the
        drawing has none."""
    @staticmethod
    def SuggestName(imageDictionary: DxfDBDictionary, newImagePathName: str) -> str:
        """Gets a name for a definition of a picture in a dictionary of images, as AutoCAD 2021's SuggestName gives
        it: the file's name without its folder or extension, px43 for C:\\pictures\\px43.png and Photo 1 for
        pictures\\Photo 1.JPG; and where the dictionary has that name, letters of either case the same, the name
        and _1, or _2 and on, the first it has not."""
    def ToString(self) -> str:
        """Gives the definition as a line for debugging: its type, its handle and its path."""

class DxfRasterVariables(DxfDBObject):
    """The RASTERVARIABLES of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's RasterVariables: how the images of the drawing are shown, the
    entry ACAD_IMAGE_VARS of the named object dictionary, which AutoCAD 2021 writes once a drawing holds an image
    or IMAGEFRAME is first changed (DxfRasterVariables.GetRasterVariables):
    db.NamedObjectsDictionary.GetAt(\"ACAD_IMAGE_VARS\")."""
    @property
    def ImageFrame(self) -> DxfFrameSetting:
        """Gets or sets whether the frames of the images are shown (group 70), as AutoCAD's ImageFrame: written as
        the number of the setting, 0 to 3, as AutoCAD 2021 writes it; DxfFrameSetting.ImageFrameOff where the
        record gives none, DxfFrameSetting.ImageFrameInvalid for a number outside 0 to 3."""
    @ImageFrame.setter
    def ImageFrame(self, value: DxfFrameSetting) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ImageQuality(self) -> DxfImageQuality:
        """Gets or sets how finely the images are shown (group 71), as AutoCAD's ImageQuality: draft (0) or high
        (1); high where the record gives none, DxfImageQuality.Invalid for another number."""
    @ImageQuality.setter
    def ImageQuality(self, value: DxfImageQuality) -> None: ...
    @property
    def UserScale(self) -> DxfUnit:
        """Gets or sets the unit images are scaled in where the drawing gives none (group 72), as AutoCAD's
        UserScale: none (0) where the record gives none, and for a number outside 0 to 20."""
    @UserScale.setter
    def UserScale(self, value: DxfUnit) -> None: ...
    @staticmethod
    def GetRasterVariables(database: DxfDatabase) -> DxfRasterVariables:
        """Gets the variables of images of a drawing, as AutoCAD's RasterVariables.GetRasterVariables: its entry
        ACAD_IMAGE_VARS, made where it has none, as AutoCAD 2021 makes it when IMAGEFRAME is first changed in a
        drawing with no image yet: frames shown (70 of 1), pictures shown finely (71 of 1), and the unit images
        are inserted in (72) that of the drawing ($INSUNITS), as AutoCAD numbers it there: 1 for millimetres, 2
        centimetres, 3 metres, 4 kilometres, 5 inches, 6 feet, 7 yards, 8 miles, 0 for none or another unit; the
        class RASTERVARIABLES listed. A metric drawing of millimetres is given 70 1, 71 1, 72 1."""
    def ToString(self) -> str:
        """Gives the variables as a line for debugging: their type, their handle and their three settings."""

class DxfRay(DxfCurve):
    """A RAY of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's Ray: the half line from DxfRay.BasePoint without end along DxfRay.UnitDir,
    in world coordinates."""
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        """Initializes a ray from the origin along the x axis, as AutoCAD's new Ray(), on layer 0 in no file; give
        it its base point and direction before it is drawn."""
    @property
    def Area(self) -> float:
        """Gets nought: a ray closes no area."""
    @property
    def BasePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets the point the ray starts from (groups 10, 20, 30), in world coordinates, as AutoCAD's
        BasePoint; the origin where the record gives none."""
    @BasePoint.setter
    def BasePoint(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Closed(self) -> bool:
        """Gets false: a ray is not closed."""
    @property
    def EndParam(self) -> float:
        """Gets the parameter at the end of the ray: infinite, as it runs without end."""
    @property
    def EndPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Refuses: a ray runs without end, and has no end point, as AutoCAD's has none."""
    @EndPoint.setter
    def EndPoint(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def SecondPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets a second point of the ray, as AutoCAD's SecondPoint: the base point and the direction; set,
        the direction is made the way from the base point to it."""
    @SecondPoint.setter
    def SecondPoint(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def StartPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets the point the ray starts from: its DxfRay.BasePoint."""
    @StartPoint.setter
    def StartPoint(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def UnitDir(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets or sets the direction of the ray (groups 11, 21, 31), as AutoCAD's UnitDir: as the file holds it, of
        unit length in a file AutoCAD wrote; (0, 0, 1) where the record gives none."""
    @UnitDir.setter
    def UnitDir(self, value: GeoVector3) -> None: ...
    @overload
    def Extend(self, newParameter: float) -> None:
        """Extends the ray back along itself to a parameter below nought, as AutoCAD's Extend: its base point is
        moved back there, so that its parameters start anew from it."""
    @overload
    def Extend(self, extendStart: bool, toPoint: GeoPoint3) -> None:
        """Extends the ray back to a point on the line through it, as AutoCAD's Extend: the base point moved
        there."""
    def GetClosestPointTo(self, givenPoint: GeoPoint3, extend: bool) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point of the ray nearest a point, as AutoCAD's GetClosestPointTo: on the ray, or on the infinite
        line through it where it is extended."""
    def GetDistAtPoint(self, point: GeoPoint3) -> float:
        """Gets the distance from the base point to a point of the ray."""
    def GetDistanceAtParameter(self, value: float) -> float:
        """Gets the distance from the base point at a parameter: the parameter itself."""
    def GetFirstDerivative(self, value: float) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets the derivative of the ray at a parameter, as AutoCAD's GetFirstDerivative: its direction made of
        unit length."""
    def GetOffsetCurves(self, offsetDist: float) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfCurve]:
        """Refuses: a ray has no plane of its own to be offset in; DxfRay.GetOffsetCurvesGivenPlaneNormal takes
        one."""
    def GetOffsetCurvesGivenPlaneNormal(
        self,
        planeNormal: GeoVector3,
        offsetDist: float,
    ) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfCurve]:
        """Gets the ray at a distance from this one in the plane of a normal, as AutoCAD's
        GetOffsetCurvesGivenPlaneNormal: to the left of its direction seen from the tip of the normal where the
        distance is above nought, as a DxfLine is offset, AutoCAD 2021's side for a line."""
    def GetParameterAtDistance(self, dist: float) -> float:
        """Gets the parameter at a distance from the base point: the distance itself."""
    def GetParameterAtPoint(self, point: GeoPoint3) -> float:
        """Gets the parameter at a point of the ray, the distance from the base point, as AutoCAD's
        GetParameterAtPoint."""
    def GetPointAtDist(self, value: float) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point at a distance from the base point."""
    def GetPointAtParameter(self, value: float) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point at a parameter, the distance from the base point, as AutoCAD's GetPointAtParameter."""
    def GetSecondDerivative(self, value: float) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets the second derivative of the ray: nought, as a ray does not bend."""
    def GetSplitCurves(
        self,
        parameters: System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[float],
    ) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfCurve]:
        """Gets the pieces the ray is cut into at parameters, as AutoCAD's GetSplitCurves: lines from the base point
        to the first parameter and on to the next, then a ray from the last, all of the same look in no file; the
        parameters taken in increasing order, one at the base point or within the point tolerance of another
        cutting nothing."""
    def ReverseCurve(self) -> None:
        """Refuses, as AutoCAD does: a ray runs one way from its base point, and turned it would be another ray."""
    def SetFromGeCurve(self, geCurve: object) -> None:
        """Gives the ray the origin and direction of a GeoRay3, as AutoCAD's SetFromGeCurve, or of a GeoRay2 at z =
        0, each written as DxfWriter writes one."""
    @overload
    def ToGeoRay2(self) -> GeoRay2:
        """Gets the ray in the plane, as DxfReader reads it with DxfReadOptions.PlanAs2D within the default
        tolerance: the ray from (0, 0, 0) along (3, 4, 0) is the GeoRay2 from (0, 0) along (0.6, 0.8). One whose
        origin is at a height, or whose direction rises, does not lie on the floor, and is refused."""
    @overload
    def ToGeoRay2(self, tolerance: Tolerance) -> GeoRay2:
        """Gets the ray in the plane, as DxfRay.ToGeoRay2 does, within a tolerance, which says whether it has a
        direction."""
    def ToGeoRay3(self) -> GeoRay3:
        """Gets the ray as the library's, as AutoCAD's GetGeCurve and the AutoCAD bridge's ToGeoRay3 give it: the
        shape DxfEntity.GetGeometry gives, to the bit. The ray from (0, 0, 0) along (3, 4, 0) is the GeoRay3 from
        there along (0.6, 0.8, 0)."""

class DxfReadOptions(System.Object):
    """How DxfReader reads a DXF file: whether a drawing in the plan comes back as shapes of the plane, whether its
    numbers are scaled to millimetres, and the tolerance that says which entities have no shape to them."""
    def __init__(self) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ExpandBlocks(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether each INSERT is read as the entities of its block, placed where it puts them; true by
        default. False leaves the INSERTs out, counted in DxfDocument.Skipped: the blocks are read into
        DxfDocument.Blocks either way."""
    @ExpandBlocks.setter
    def ExpandBlocks(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def KeepGroups(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether each entity keeps every group of its record as the file has it, in DxfShape.Groups;
        true by default. False leaves them empty, which a large file reads in less memory: the shapes and the
        look of the entities are read either way."""
    @KeepGroups.setter
    def KeepGroups(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def MaxPlacedEntities(self) -> int:
        """Gets or sets how many entities the INSERTs may place from blocks in one reading, counted across the
        drawing and the blocks read for DxfDocument.Blocks; 2 000 000 by default."""
    @MaxPlacedEntities.setter
    def MaxPlacedEntities(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    @property
    def PlanAs2D(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether an entity that lies on the floor is read as the shape of the plane it is. False by
        default, which reads every entity as the shape of space it is."""
    @PlanAs2D.setter
    def PlanAs2D(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def SupportFolders(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IList[str]:
        """Gets or sets the folders a DWG's files of shapes are looked for in, in their order, as AutoCAD looks in
        its support folders; empty by default. Used where DwgReader reads a DWG."""
    @SupportFolders.setter
    def SupportFolders(self, value: System.Collections.Generic.IList[str]) -> None: ...
    @property
    def ToMillimeters(self) -> bool:
        """Gets or sets whether the coordinates and sizes are scaled to millimetres by the unit the file says it is
        in (DxfDocument.Units): a drawing in metres has its numbers times 1 000. False by default, which keeps
        the numbers as the file prints them."""
    @ToMillimeters.setter
    def ToMillimeters(self, value: bool) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Tolerance(self) -> Tolerance:
        """Gets or sets the tolerance that says which entities have no shape to them and which four corners of a
        3DFACE lie in one plane; Tolerance.Default unless set."""
    @Tolerance.setter
    def Tolerance(self, value: Tolerance) -> None: ...

class DxfReader(System.Object):
    """Reads a DXF file into the library's shapes: what DxfWriter writes, back to the bit where the file holds the
    number, and what AutoCAD and the other CAD programs write of the same kinds, from R12 to R2018."""
    @staticmethod
    def Parse(text: str, options: DxfReadOptions = ...) -> DxfDocument:
        """Reads a DXF file from its text."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Read(stream: System.IO.Stream, options: DxfReadOptions = ...) -> DxfDocument:
        """Reads a DXF file from a stream, from where the stream stands to its end."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def Read(path: str, options: DxfReadOptions = ...) -> DxfDocument:
        """Reads a DXF file from a path."""

class DxfRectangle3d(System.ValueType):
    """The four corners of a frame in world coordinates, as AutoCAD's Rectangle3d: where an OLE object is shown
    (DxfOle2Frame.Position3d). The corners are as the drawing holds them, not checked to be square: a picture
    83.58 by 30.67 laid along x from (15.72, 12.19, 0) has its upper left corner at (15.72, 42.85, 0) and its
    lower right at (99.29, 12.19, 0)."""
    def __init__(
        self,
        upperLeft: GeoPoint3,
        upperRight: GeoPoint3,
        lowerLeft: GeoPoint3,
        lowerRight: GeoPoint3,
    ) -> None:
        """Initializes the corners, in the order of AutoCAD's Rectangle3d(upperLeft, upperRight, lowerLeft,
        lowerRight): the two upper ones, then the two lower ones, each from the left."""
    @property
    def LowerLeft(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the lower left corner, as AutoCAD's LowerLeft."""
    @property
    def LowerRight(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the lower right corner, as AutoCAD's LowerRight."""
    @property
    def UpperLeft(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the upper left corner, as AutoCAD's UpperLeft."""
    @property
    def UpperRight(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the upper right corner, as AutoCAD's UpperRight."""
    def ToString(self) -> str:
        """Gives the corners as a line for debugging, the upper two, then the lower two."""

class DxfRegionLoop(System.Object):
    """One loop of a REGION: the curves that bound it, joined end to end in the order the loop runs, as AutoCAD's
    Explode gives them for the region."""
    @property
    def Area(self) -> float:
        """Gets the area the loop encloses, not taking away its holes: a square of side 10 gives 100, hole or
        not."""
    @property
    def Curves(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfCurve]:
        """Gets the curves of the loop in the order it runs, each a new entity in no drawing; the same list on each
        call."""
    @property
    def IsHole(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether the loop is a hole in the face it bounds."""
    @property
    def Perimeter(self) -> float:
        """Gets the length of the loop: a circle of radius 7 gives 43.9823."""

class DxfRegionShape(System.Object):
    """The shape of a planar REGION: the loops that bound its faces, outer loops and holes, with the area and the
    perimeter AutoCAD's Region gives for it."""
    @property
    def Area(self) -> float:
        """Gets the area of the region: that of its outer loops less that of its holes, as AutoCAD's Region.Area."""
    @property
    def Loops(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfRegionLoop]:
        """Gets the loops of every face, the holes of a face before its outer loop."""
    @property
    def Normal(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets the unit normal of the plane of the first face, as AutoCAD's Region.Normal: (0, 0, 1) for a region
        lying flat on the XY plane."""
    @property
    def Perimeter(self) -> float:
        """Gets the perimeter of the region: the length of every loop, holes too, as AutoCAD's Region.Perimeter."""
    @staticmethod
    def Create(
        outer: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfCurve],
        holes: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfCurve]],
        tolerance: Tolerance,
    ) -> DxfRegionShape:
        """Makes the shape of one flat face from the curves of its outer loop and of each hole. The curves of a loop
        may come in any order and any way round, the lines and arcs of a loop joining end to end within the point
        tolerance; a circle, a whole ellipse or a closed polyline is a loop of itself. The outer loop is made to
        run counter-clockwise about the normal of its plane (+Z for a loop that lies flat on the XY plane) and a
        hole clockwise."""
    @staticmethod
    def Intersect(
        shapes: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfRegionShape],
        tolerance: Tolerance,
    ) -> DxfRegionShape:
        """Gets what every one of the shapes covers: a circle of radius 10 about (0, 0) and one about (10, 0) have a
        lens of area 122.84 and perimeter 41.89, two arcs."""
    def IsCoplanarWith(self, other: DxfRegionShape, tolerance: Tolerance) -> bool:
        """Gets whether every edge of the shape lies in the plane of the first face of another, within the point
        tolerance."""
    @staticmethod
    def Subtract(
        shapes: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfRegionShape],
        tools: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfRegionShape],
        tolerance: Tolerance,
    ) -> DxfRegionShape:
        """Gets what the shapes cover less what the tools cover: a box 40 by 30 less a circle of radius 10 centred
        on its right edge has area 1 042.92 and perimeter 151.42, the circle a notch of one arc in the right
        side; less a circle of radius 5 inside it, a face of two loops, the circle a hole."""
    @staticmethod
    def Unite(shapes: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[DxfRegionShape], tolerance: Tolerance) -> DxfRegionShape:
        """Gets what any of the shapes covers: a box 40 by 30 and a circle of radius 10 centred on its right edge
        give a shape of area 1 357.08 whose one loop is five lines and a half circle, the circle still a circle."""

class DxfRepair(System.Object):
    """One thing found wrong with a drawing by DxfDatabase.Recover or DxfDatabase.Audit: its kind, a sentence saying
    what and where, the line of the file or the handle of the record, and whether it was fixed. \"Line 7 is not a
    group code ('1O') and was left out.\" is a repair of the kind DxfRepairKind.BadGroupCode on line 7, fixed."""
    @property
    def Handle(self) -> str:
        """Gets the handle of the record it was found in; null where it is said by line or the record has none."""
    @property
    def IsFixed(self) -> bool:
        """Gets whether it was fixed: false for what is only reported, as an INSERT of a block the drawing does not
        define, and for everything DxfDatabase.Audit finds without fixing."""
    @property
    def Kind(self) -> DxfRepairKind:
        """Gets what was wrong."""
    @property
    def Line(self) -> int:
        """Gets the line of the file it was found on, counted from 1; 0 where it is said by handle or of the whole
        file."""
    @property
    def Message(self) -> str:
        """Gets a sentence saying what was wrong, where, and what was done about it."""
    def ToString(self) -> str:
        """Gives the message."""

class DxfRepairKind(System.Enum):
    """What was wrong with a drawing, as DxfDatabase.Recover and DxfDatabase.Audit name it in a DxfRepair, in the
    order a file is read: first the bytes and lines, then the sections, the records, the handles and the tables."""
    BadGroupCode: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A line where a group code should stand that is not a whole number from 0 to 1071: left out, the next line
    read as a code."""
    BadNumber: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A group of a number whose value is no number: the number it begins with, or nought."""
    BadOwner: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """An owner (group 330) that names no record: the entity's block, the vertex's polyline or the entry's table
    named instead."""
    BrokenDictionaryEntry: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """An entry of a DICTIONARY that is broken, a name with no pointer after it, a pointer with no name before it,
    or a pointer that is not a handle: left out. A pointer to an object the file does not hold is not broken:
    AutoCAD writes those of objects it leaves out of a DXF."""
    DuplicateHandle: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A handle two records have: the later given a new one, the records it owns pointed at it."""
    Encoding: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """Text in the wrong code page: a file of R2007 or later whose bytes are not UTF-8, read in the page its header
    names and written as UTF-8; or a header naming a page a DXF cannot be in, named ANSI_1252 instead."""
    HandseedTooLow: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A $HANDSEED not above every handle, or missing: set above them."""
    LineEnds: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """Lines ended by a carriage return alone, as an old Macintosh writes them: read as lines, written with line
    feeds."""
    MissingBlock: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """An INSERT of a block the drawing does not define: kept, drawing nothing."""
    MissingDimStyle: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A dimension style a dimension, a leader or a tolerance names that the table does not list: added with the
    defaults."""
    MissingEndBlk: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A BLOCK with no ENDBLK before the next BLOCK or the end of the section: its ENDBLK written."""
    MissingHandle: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A record of a file of R13 or later with no handle, or one that is not hexadecimal: given a new one."""
    MissingLayer: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A layer an entity is on that the layer table does not list: added with the defaults."""
    MissingLinetype: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A linetype an entity names that the linetype table does not list: added, drawn solid."""
    MissingSection: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A section missing: ENTITIES added empty; a HEADER naming R2000 added to a file whose records are of R13 or
    later; TABLES, BLOCKS or OBJECTS of such a file reported, not made."""
    MissingSeqEnd: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A POLYLINE, or an INSERT with attributes, with no SEQEND after its vertices or attributes: its SEQEND
    written."""
    MissingTextStyle: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A text style a text names that the style table does not list: added with the defaults."""
    MissingValue: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A group code on the last line of the file with no value after it: left out."""
    NonFiniteNumber: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A number that is not finite (NaN, an infinity): the entity left out, nought elsewhere."""
    SectionOrder: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """Sections out of AutoCAD's order (HEADER, CLASSES, TABLES, BLOCKS, ENTITIES, OBJECTS): put in that order."""
    SectionStructure: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A section not closed before the next opens, an ENDSEC that closes nothing, a section with no name, or records
    outside every section: closed, left out, named from what it holds, or moved into ENTITIES where they are
    entities."""
    Truncated: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A file cut short, with no EOF: the section it ends in closed and the EOF written."""
    UnknownEntity: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """An entity of a type neither AutoCAD's own nor named in the CLASSES section: kept as it is."""
    Unreadable: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """What was left after the repairs still could not be read: only its entities kept (fixed), or an empty drawing
    (not fixed); or nothing of a DXF was found in the file, not one record (not fixed), the drawing empty."""
    WrongLoopCount: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A HATCH whose count of boundary paths (group 91) is not the number of its paths: set to that number."""
    WrongVertexCount: ClassVar[DxfRepairKind]
    """A LWPOLYLINE whose count of vertices (group 90) is not the number of its vertices: set to that number."""
    def __init__(self, value: int) -> None: ...
    def __int__(self) -> int: ...

class DxfRepairReport(System.Object):
    """What DxfDatabase.Recover or DxfDatabase.Audit found wrong with a drawing, in the order it was found: each a
    DxfRepair, with how many there are and how many were fixed. A sound file gives an empty report."""
    @property
    def Count(self) -> int:
        """Gets how many things were found."""
    @property
    def FixedCount(self) -> int:
        """Gets how many of them were fixed."""
    @property
    def Repairs(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfRepair]:
        """Gets what was found, in the order it was found."""
    @property
    def Summary(self) -> str:
        """Gets the report in one sentence, as AutoCAD ends its audit: \"No errors found.\" for a sound file, else
        how many were found and fixed, \"3 errors found, 3 fixed.\""""
    def CountOf(self, kind: DxfRepairKind) -> int:
        """Counts what was found of one kind."""
    def ToString(self) -> str:
        """Gives the summary."""

class DxfRotatedDimension(DxfDimension):
    """A rotated dimension of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's RotatedDimension: the distance between two points measured
    along a direction, level, upright or turned; a DIMENSION of kind 0."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        """Initializes a level dimension of the origin to the origin, as AutoCAD's new RotatedDimension(), in the
        style Standard."""
    @overload
    def __init__(
        self,
        rotation: float,
        line1Point: GeoPoint3,
        line2Point: GeoPoint3,
        dimensionLinePoint: GeoPoint3,
        dimensionText: str,
        dimensionStyle: DxfDimStyleTableRecord,
    ) -> None:
        """Initializes a rotated dimension, as AutoCAD's new RotatedDimension(rotation, line1Point, line2Point,
        dimensionLinePoint, dimensionText, dimensionStyle), in no file until it is added to one; it needs its
        DxfDimension.DimBlock before it is."""
    @property
    def DimLinePoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets a point of the dimension line (groups 10, 20, 30), as AutoCAD's DimLinePoint, in world
        coordinates."""
    @DimLinePoint.setter
    def DimLinePoint(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Measurement(self) -> float:
        """Gets the distance between the two points along DxfRotatedDimension.Rotation, as AutoCAD's Measurement,
        the direction taken in the plane of the normal: 96.60 from (0, 0, 0) to (100, 20, 0) along 30 degrees."""
    @property
    def Oblique(self) -> float:
        """Gets or sets the angle of the extension lines from the dimension line (group 52, in degrees), as
        AutoCAD's Oblique: in radians; nought where the record gives none, the extension lines then square to the
        line. The extension lines run at DxfRotatedDimension.Rotation and this together from the x axis: AutoCAD
        2021 gives an Oblique of 30 to a dimension rotated 30 that DIMEDIT slants to 60."""
    @Oblique.setter
    def Oblique(self, value: float) -> None: ...
    @property
    def Rotation(self) -> float:
        """Gets or sets the direction measured along (group 50, in degrees, in the plane of the normal), as
        AutoCAD's Rotation: in radians, nought along x, pi / 2 along y; nought where the record gives none."""
    @Rotation.setter
    def Rotation(self, value: float) -> None: ...
    @property
    def XLine1Point(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets where the first extension line starts (groups 13, 23, 33), as AutoCAD's XLine1Point, in
        world coordinates."""
    @XLine1Point.setter
    def XLine1Point(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...
    @property
    def XLine2Point(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets or sets where the second extension line starts (groups 14, 24, 34), as AutoCAD's XLine2Point, in
        world coordinates."""
    @XLine2Point.setter
    def XLine2Point(self, value: GeoPoint3) -> None: ...

