    @overload
    def ToPolylineWithPrecision(self, precision: int, bConvertAsArcs: bool, bToLWPolyline: bool) -> DxfCurve:
        """Gets the polyline that runs along the spline within a precision, as AutoCAD's ToPolylineWithPrecision. Of
        lines, as AutoCAD 2021 makes it: the spline's whole parameter range, from its start to its end, halved
        again and again until the spline's points halfway, a quarter and three quarters along each piece's
        parameter are no farther from the chord's points there than the larger of one over the spline's sharpest
        bend and a ten-thousandth of its length, over the square of one more than the precision, max(1 / M, L /
        10 000) / (p + 1)^2, M the largest length of the spline's second derivative by its parameter; each piece
        a segment. AutoCAD's 156 counts at hand, of cubics, a quadratic, a quartic, quintics and rational cubics,
        at 0 to 99 (its plugin runs v4 to v7 and D32), are the rule's but 9, each within 3 of AutoCAD's, 7 of
        them of rational cubics: a quintic Bezier gives 86, 478 and 7 929 vertices at 0, 5 and 99 and the same 10
        times its size, a hairpin cubic of 100 by 1 over the knots 0 to 1 129 at 0, where its length decides, and
        over 0 to 100 5, where its bend does, and an S of three spans whose middle lies on its chord 173. The
        rule gives AutoCAD's counts of vertices for the three cubics of its plugin runs v4 and v5 at every
        precision tried: the cubic of one span on (0, 0), (10, 10), (20, 10), (30, 0), whose bend is 60
        everywhere, 33, 65, 129, 257 and 4 097 vertices at 0, 1, 3, 10 and 99; the cubic of two spans on (0, 40),
        (10, 50), (20, 50), (30, 40), (40, 30), 50 at 0, 513 at 10 and 4 750 at 99; the cubic of three spans on
        (0, 0), (10, 10), (20, 10), (30, 0), (40, -10), (50, 0), 78 at 0 and 7 562 at 99. The sharpest bend is
        read at the ends of each span of the knots and at seven points between, which for a cubic, whose second
        derivative runs straight along a span, is its largest; a piece is halved no more than 20 times over and
        no finer than the rounding of the spline's largest coordinate, and a straight spline is one segment. The
        rule gives AutoCAD's counts for a quadratic of three spans and a cubic of a double knot too (29, 342 and
        2 732, and 76, 933 and 8 011 at 0, 10 and 99), a spline of degree 5 (96 at 0) and a rational one (130 at
        0, 1 378 at 10 where AutoCAD gives 1 377). A closed spline has its last vertex on its first, the polyline
        closed; one closed, or of the flag 2 of its 70 (the periodic of the DXF reference, which AutoCAD writes
        on its closed splines of a smooth seam), that runs through fit points, or that AutoCAD keeps by its fit
        points, the flag 1024 of its 70 set (its 3115 of a periodic cubic, written with no fit points), has each
        of its knots, one after another, in the place of the vertex of the halving nearest it, the later of two
        as near, a knot taking the place another took before it, as AutoCAD 2021 gave them: the closed cubic
        through (0, 0), (40, 0), (50, 30) and (10, 25), its knots the lengths of the chords, is those four points
        and the first again at 0, and 48 vertices at 10, the range halved into 64ths and the knot 40 standing in
        the place of the 64th at 39.05; through (0, 0), (40, 0), (40.5, 0.5), (50, 30) and (10, 25) it is at 0
        the vertices at 0, 40.71, 71.70, 112.01 and its end, the knot 40.71 in the place the knot 40 took. The
        same spline of no fit points and no flag 1024, its 70 of 3, is the halving alone, as AutoCAD 2021 gave
        it: (0, 0), (34.42, -3.51), (50.86, 28.40), (18.15, 30.49) and the first again at 0. AutoCAD's closed
        cubic not periodic through (0, 0), (30, 0), (30, 15) and (20, 15), a corner at its seam (70 1065), has
        its knots in place as well: at 0 (0, 0), (22.66, -5.01), (30, 15), (20, 15) and the first again, the
        knots 45 and 55 for the quarters 40 and 60 (its D32 run, where 35 of the 36 polylines of six such cubics
        at 0 to 10 are the library's). Each arc is bent as the piece the halving made, its first, from (0, 0) to
        (40, 0) at 0, by the turn of the tangent over the first quarter of the range. Of arcs, for a flat spline,
        the same vertices, each segment the arc that turns as the spline's tangent turns along it, its bulge the
        tangent of a quarter of that turn, as AutoCAD 2021 makes them: the cubic of one span at 0 gives 33
        vertices, its first arc, from (0, 0) to (0.9375, 0.908), of bulge -0.00806, the spline's tangent turning
