class DxfTable(DxfEntity):
    """The cells of a table walked, their values with their kinds and formats, their look set, their overrides, and
    the cell a point hits, as AutoCAD's Table has them.

    What the Table Cell tab of AutoCAD 2021 sets of a single cell beyond its text and look: its state (Cell
    Locking), a block put into it (Insert Block) and a field or formula it shows (Insert Field, Insert Formula).

    The TABLECONTENT, TABLEGEOMETRY and round trip AutoCAD 2021 makes of a table when it reads the file, made
    when the drawing is saved (DxfDatabase.Save), so that AutoCAD has nothing to build or mend.

    The TABLECONTENT AutoCAD keeps for a table, kept in step with the table's rows, columns and merged cells, and
    made for a table of none when a cell of it is linked, as AutoCAD 2021 writes it.

    A table of a DXF file, as AutoCAD's Table: an ACAD_TABLE, its rows and columns, the text, value, kind and
    look of each cell, the cells merged, and the anonymous block (*T12) AutoCAD drew it with.

    The links of a table's cells to data, as AutoCAD's Table keeps them: a range of cells filled from a
    DxfDataLink of the drawing, the link named by the range's top left cell.

    The lines of a table's grid, as AutoCAD's Table reads and sets them: the edges of a cell, each the cell's own
    override with its flag, and the lines of the rows of a kind, the table's own with its flags 94 to 96.

    What rows and columns put in change beyond their own cells, as AutoCAD 2021's Table changes it: the title
    merged anew over columns put in at its edge, and the kinds of rows a row put in at the title or the header
    moves on.

    A table made in code, and the anonymous block it is drawn with drawn anew from its cells.

    The structure of a table changed as AutoCAD's Table changes it: rows and columns put in and taken out, cells
    merged and unmerged, cells copied from another table and filled in a series, and the table given back to its
    style."""
    def __init__(
        self,
        position: GeoPoint3,
        numRows: int,
        numColumns: int,
        rowHeight: float,
        columnWidth: float,
    ) -> None:
        """Initializes a table in no file, as AutoCAD's new Table() given its Position and SetSize: rows of one
        height and columns of one width, every cell an empty text cell that takes its look from the table style,
        to be added to a drawing by DxfBlockTableRecord.AppendEntity. Added, it names the drawing's current table
        style (DxfDatabase.Tablestyle, where the drawing has it), its first row is merged across the table as
        AutoCAD's title is, and it is drawn in a new anonymous block (*T1 and on) by
        DxfTable.RecomputeTableBlock: new DxfTable(new GeoPoint3(0, 0, 0), 6, 5, 9, 63.5) is a table 317.5 wide
        and 54 high, its top left at the origin, its title, header and four rows of data in five columns."""
    @property
    def BlockTableRecord(self) -> DxfBlockTableRecord:
        """Gets the anonymous block AutoCAD drew the table with (group 2), as AutoCAD's BlockTableRecord gives its
        id: *T12; null where the drawing has no block of its name."""
    @property
    def Cells(self) -> DxfCellRange:
        """Gets every cell of the table as a range, as AutoCAD's Cells: table.Cells[1, 0] is the cell of the second
        row and the first column, a DxfCell that reads and sets it; the range of a table of 3 rows and 2 columns
        is (0, 0) to (2, 1)."""
    @property
    def Columns(self) -> System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList[DxfColumn]:
        """Gets the columns of the table, as AutoCAD's Columns: table.Columns[1].Width is the width of the second,
        read and set as DxfTable.ColumnWidth and DxfTable.SetColumnWidth do; as many as DxfTable.NumColumns."""
    @property
    def Direction(self) -> GeoVector3:
        """Gets the direction of the table's rows (groups 11, 21, 31), as AutoCAD's Direction; (1, 0, 0) where the
        record gives none."""
    @property
    def FlowDirection(self) -> DxfFlowDirection:
        """Gets which way the rows follow one another (its own 70, after its cells or in its head: 0 down, 1 up), as
        AutoCAD's FlowDirection: DxfFlowDirection.TopToBottom or DxfFlowDirection.BottomToTop; down where the
        table gives none of its own."""
    @property
    def Height(self) -> float:
        """Gets the height of the table, its rows' heights together, as AutoCAD's Height: 26 for rows 10, 8 and 8
        high."""
    @property
    def HorizontalCellMargin(self) -> float:
        """Gets the margin left and right of a cell's content (its own 40), as AutoCAD's HorizontalCellMargin; where
        the table gives none of its own, its table style's (the style's 40), and where the drawing has no style,
        that of AutoCAD's own Standard, 1.5 in a drawing of millimetres and 0.06 in one of inches, as AutoCAD
        2021 read a table of none of its own by its style's margin of 2 as 2 and by its Standard as 1.5 (D28d
